":"managed","start":411.6,"end":412.44},{"word":"to","start":412.44,"end":412.64},{"word":"do","start":412.64,"end":412.76},{"word":"a","start":412.76,"end":412.92},{"word":"plank","start":412.92,"end":413.3},{"word":"for","start":413.3,"end":413.92},{"word":"over","start":413.92,"end":414.24},{"word":"nine","start":414.24,"end":414.68},{"word":"hours","start":414.68,"end":415.86},{"word":"on","start":415.86,"end":418.04},{"word":"his","start":418.04,"end":418.34},{"word":"CRPS","start":418.34,"end":418.98},{"word":"arm.","start":418.98,"end":419.44}],"textKo":"다니엘은 CRPS 팔로 9시간 이상 플랭크를 해냈다.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":83,"start":419.44,"end":422.28,"textEn":"Now, think about that for a minute.","words":[{"word":"Now,","start":419.44,"end":421.0},{"word":"think","start":421.0,"end":421.24},{"word":"about","start":421.24,"end":421.5},{"word":"that","start":421.5,"end":421.72},{"word":"for","start":421.72,"end":421.94},{"word":"a","start":421.94,"end":422.1},{"word":"minute.","start":422.1,"end":422.28}],"textKo":"잠깐 생각해보자.","listenDifficulty":2},{"index":84,"start":423.84,"end":431.44,"textEn":"The most physically and mentally challenging exercises helped one of the most painful conditions.","words":[{"word":"The","start":423.43,"end":423.94},{"word":"most","start":423.94,"end":424.68},{"word":"physically","start":424.68,"end":425.3},{"word":"and","start":425.3,"end":425.76},{"word":"mentally","start":425.76,"end":426.28},{"word":"challenging","start":426.28,"end":426.9},{"word":"exercises","start":426.9,"end":427.72},{"word":"helped","start":427.72,"end":428.74},{"word":"one","start":428.74,"end":429.7},{"word":"of","start":429.7,"end":429.82},{"word":"the","start":429.82,"end":429.96},{"word":"most","start":429.96,"end":430.24},{"word":"painful","start":430.24,"end":430.74},{"word":"conditions.","start":430.74,"end":431.44}],"textKo":"신체적으로도 정신적으로도 가장 힘든 운동들이 가장 고통스러운 상태 중 하나를 도와주었다.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":85,"start":433.28,"end":439.8,"textEn":"Now we have evidence that an important part of the answer lies in BDNF.","words":[{"word":"Now","start":432.93,"end":433.44},{"word":"we","start":433.44,"end":433.92},{"word":"have","start":433.92,"end":434.3},{"word":"evidence","start":434.3,"end":435.22},{"word":"that","start":435.22,"end":435.92},{"word":"an","start":435.92,"end":436.12},{"word":"important","start":436.12,"end":436.5},{"word":"part","start":436.5,"end":436.76},{"word":"of","start":436.76,"end":436.9},{"word":"the","start":436.9,"end":437.02},{"word":"answer","start":437.02,"end":437.48},{"word":"lies","start":437.48,"end":438.4},{"word":"in","start":438.4,"end":439.02},{"word":"BDNF.","start":439.02,"end":439.8}],"textKo":"이제 BDNF에 답변의 중요한 부분이 있다는 증거가 있다.","listenDifficulty":2},{"index":86,"start":439.8,"end":448.12,"textEn":"In August of 2024, an article appeared in experimental neurobiology titled,","words":[{"word":"In","start":439.8,"end":441.22},{"word":"August","start":441.22,"end":441.7},{"word":"of","start":441.7,"end":442.3},{"word":"2024,","start":442.3,"end":443.12},{"word":"an","start":443.6,"end":444.1},{"word":"article","start":444.1,"end":444.46},{"word":"appeared","start":444.46,"end":445.0},{"word":"in","start":445.0,"end":445.24},{"word":"experimental","start":445.24,"end":445.92},{"word":"neurobiology","start":445.92,"end":447.12},{"word":"titled,","start":447.12,"end":448.12}],"textKo":"2024년 8월, 실험 신경생물학 저널에 실린 글 제목은,","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":87,"start":448.58,"end":452.52,"textEn":"Modulation of BDNF by Physical Exercise.","words":[{"word":"Modulation","start":448.58,"end":449.52},{"word":"of","start":449.52,"end":449.96},{"word":"BDNF","start":449.96,"end":450.66},{"word":"by","start":450.66,"end":451.4},{"word":"Physical","start":451.4,"end":451.88},{"word":"Exercise.","start":451.88,"end":452.52}],"textKo":"물리적 운동을 통한 BDNF 조절.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":88,"start":453.04,"end":458.48,"textEn":"They found exercise doubled the level of BDNF.","words":[{"word":"They","start":453.04,"end":454.16},{"word":"found","start":454.16,"end":454.56},{"word":"exercise","start":454.56,"end":455.5},{"word":"doubled","start":455.5,"end":456.46},{"word":"the","start":456.46,"end":457.04},{"word":"level","start":457.04,"end":457.42},{"word":"of","start":457.42,"end":457.72},{"word":"BDNF.","start":457.72,"end":458.48}],"textKo":"그들은 운동이 BDNF의 수준을 두 배로 만들었다고 밝혔다.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":89,"start":460.6,"end":467.7,"textEn":"I am here to raise awareness so that this relationship between exercise, BDNF,","words":[{"word":"I","start":460.6,"end":461.4},{"word":"am","start":461.4,"end":461.58},{"word":"here","start":461.58,"end":462.04},{"word":"to","start":462.04,"end":462.68},{"word":"raise","start":462.68,"end":462.94},{"word":"awareness","start":462.94,"end":463.4},{"word":"so","start":463.4,"end":464.52},{"word":"that","start":464.52,"end":464.72},{"word":"this","start":464.72,"end":464.96},{"word":"relationship","start":464.96,"end":465.62},{"word":"between","start":465.62,"end":466.02},{"word":"exercise,","start":466.02,"end":466.9},{"word":"BDNF,","start":467.06,"end":467.7}],"textKo":"이곳에 있는 이유는 운동과 BDNF 사이의 관계에 대한 인식을 높이기 위함이다.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":90,"start":467.86,"end":472.16,"textEn":"And improving the quality of life may be studied further.","words":[{"word":"and","start":467.86,"end":468.52},{"word":"improving","start":468.52,"end":469.04},{"word":"the","start":469.04,"end":469.46},{"word":"quality","start":469.46,"end":469.9},{"word":"of","start":469.9,"end":470.08},{"word":"life","start":470.08,"end":470.48},{"word":"may","start":470.48,"end":471.2},{"word":"be","start":471.2,"end":471.34},{"word":"studied","start":471.34,"end":471.72},{"word":"further.","start":471.72,"end":472.16}],"textKo":"삶의 질을 개선하는 것에 대한 연구는 계속될 수 있습니다.","listenDifficulty":2},{"index":91,"start":473.44,"end":476.52,"textEn":"BDNF is hot in the research world.","words":[{"word":"BDNF","start":473.44,"end":474.24},{"word":"is","start":474.24,"end":474.64},{"word":"hot","start":474.64,"end":475.22},{"word":"in","start":475.22,"end":475.66},{"word":"the","start":475.66,"end":475.76},{"word":"research","start":475.76,"end":476.1},{"word":"world.","start":476.1,"end":476.52}],"textKo":"BDNF는 연구 분야에서 뜨거운 관심을 받고 있습니다.","listenDifficulty":2},{"index":92,"start":476.82,"end":484.76,"textEn":"I''m about to make it hotter. BDNF is hot in the research world.","words":[{"word":"I''m","start":476.82,"end":477.52},{"word":"about","start":477.52,"end":477.72},{"word":"to","start":477.72,"end":477.9},{"word":"make","start":477.9,"end":478.08},{"word":"it","start":478.08,"end":478.22},{"word":"hotter.","start":478.22,"end":478.5},{"word":"BDNF","start":482.68,"end":483.24},{"word":"is","start":483.24,"end":483.8},{"word":"hot","start":483.8,"end":483.8},{"word":"in","start":483.8,"end":484.72},{"word":"the","start":484.72,"end":484.72},{"word":"research","start":484.72,"end":484.76},{"word":"world.","start":484.76,"end":484.76}],"textKo":"더 뜨거워질 준비가 되었어요. BDNF는 연구 분야에서 뜨거운 관심을 받고 있습니다.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":93,"start":486.04,"end":490.9,"textEn":"George, Daniel, and my patients deserve as much.","words":[{"word":"George,","start":486.04,"end":486.6},{"word":"Daniel,","start":487.02,"end":487.52},{"word":"and","start":487.86,"end":489.16},{"word":"my","start":489.16,"end":489.32},{"word":"patients","start":489.32,"end":489.76},{"word":"deserve","start":489.76,"end":490.4},{"word":"as","start":490.4,"end":490.62},{"word":"much.","start":490.62,"end":490.9}],"textKo":"지오지, 니콜라스, 그리고 제 환자분들께서도 마찬가지입니다.","listenDifficulty":1},{"index":94,"start":491.7,"end":495.08,"textEn":"Now, I''m going to leave you with the challenge.","words":[{"word":"Now,","start":491.7,"end":492.26},{"word":"I''m","start":492.54,"end":493.1},{"word":"going","start":493.1,"end":493.28},{"word":"to","start":493.28,"end":493.52},{"word":"leave","start":493.52,"end":493.78},{"word":"you","start":493.78,"end":494.1},{"word":"with","start":494.1,"end":494.52},{"word":"the","start":494.52,"end":494.68},{"word":"challenge.","start":494.68,"end":495.08}],"textKo":"이제 여러분에게 도전 과제를 남기고자 합니다.","listenDifficulty":2},{"index":95,"start":495.44,"end":500.26,"textEn":"The next time you feel you need more grit in your life, do a plank.","words":[{"word":"The","start":495.44,"end":495.86},{"word":"next","start":495.86,"end":496.12},{"word":"time","start":496.12,"end":496.4},{"word":"you","start":496.4,"end":496.64},{"word":"feel","start":496.64,"end":496.94},{"word":"you","start":496.94,"end":497.32},{"word":"need","start":497.32,"end":497.54},{"word":"more","start":497.54,"end":497.78},{"word":"grit","start":497.78,"end":498.08},{"word":"in","start":498.08,"end":498.2},{"word":"your","start":498.2,"end":498.34},{"word":"life,","start":498.34,"end":498.72},{"word":"do","start":499.44,"end":499.86},{"word":"a","start":499.86,"end":500.0},{"word":"plank.","start":500.0,"end":500.26}],"textKo":"삶에 더 많은 인내심이 필요하다고 느낄 때 플랭크 운동을 해보세요.","listenDifficulty":3},{"index":96,"start":500.68,"end":504.04,"textEn":"If you can''t get on the floor, do it against the wall.","words":[{"word":"If","start":500.68,"end":501.24},{"word":"you","start":501.24,"end":501.42},{"word":"can''t","start":501.42,"end":501.76},{"word":"get","start":501.76,"end":501.9},{"word":"on","start":501.9,"end":502.04},{"word":"the","start":502.04,"end":502.18},{"word":"floor,","start":502.18,"end":502.5},{"word":"do","start":502.78,"end":503.22},{"word":"it","start":503.22,"end":503.36},{"word":"against","start":503.36,"end":503.62},{"word":"the","start":503.62,"end":503.8},{"word":"wall.","start":503.8,"end":504.04}],"textKo":"바닥에 앉을 수 없다면 벽에 붙어서 해보세요.","listenDifficulty":3},{"index":97,"start":504.04,"end":508.0,"textEn":"It only takes a minute, but that minute can be transformative.","words":[{"word":"It","start":504.04,"end":504.86},{"word":"only","start":504.86,"end":505.06},{"word":"takes","start":505.06,"end":505.34},{"word":"a","start":505.34,"end":505.5},{"word":"minute,","start":505.5,"end":505.74},{"word":"but","start":505.96,"end":506.16},{"word":"that","start":506.16,"end":506.38},{"word":"minute","start":506.38,"end":506.62},{"word":"can","start":506.62,"end":506.84},{"word":"be","start":506.84,"end":507.04},{"word":"transformative.","start":507.04,"end":508.0}],"textKo":"잠시만 해보는 거지만, 그 분량이 삶을 바꿀 수 있습니다.","listenDifficulty":3},{"index":98,"start":508.96,"end":509.62,"textEn":"Thank you.","words":[{"word":"Thank","start":508.96,"end":509.42},{"word":"you.","start":509.42,"end":509.62}],"textKo":"감사합니다.","listenDifficulty":3}]}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"pattern":"Present Continuous for Future Arrangements","explanation":"Used to talk about actions that are about to happen soon, often with ''be about to'' + base verb.","explanationKo":"곧 일어날 행동을 말할 때 ''be about to'' + 동사 기본형을 사용합니다.","examples":["You''re about to hold a plank. Just 60 seconds.","You''re going to collapse at 30 seconds."],"segmentIndex":1},{"pattern":"Present Simple for General Truths","explanation":"Used to state facts, general truths, or habitual actions.","explanationKo":"사실, 일반적인 진실, 또는 습관적인 행동을 나타낼 때 사용합니다.","examples":["The plank is 90% mental.","Exercise increases BDNF the most."],"segmentIndex":26},{"pattern":"Present Perfect Continuous","explanation":"Used to describe actions that started in the past and continue up to the present, often with ''have/has been + verb-ing''.","explanationKo":"과거에 시작되어 현재까지 지속되는 행동을 나타내는 데 사용합니다.","examples":["I''ve been doing clinical research for over 40 years."],"segmentIndex":47},{"pattern":"Relative Clauses","explanation":"Used to provide additional information about a noun, often introduced by ''that'' or ''which''.","explanationKo":"명사에 대한 추가 정보를 제공하는 데 사용되며, ''that'' 또는 ''which''로 시작합니다.","examples":["that mental toughness that helps people achieve extraordinary things","what we''ve learned from George"],"segmentIndex":30},{"pattern":"Negative Sentences with ''not''","explanation":"Used to express negation, often with ''am not'', ''is not'', or ''are not''.","explanationKo":"부정을 표현할 때 ''am not'', ''is not'', 또는 ''are not'' 등을 사용합니다.","examples":["In no way am I suggesting something...","You''re not going to collapse."],"segmentIndex":55},{"pattern":"Future Intention with ''be going to''","explanation":"Used to express future intentions or predictions based on current evidence.","explanationKo":"현재의 증거에 기반한 미래 의도나 예측을 표현할 때 사용합니다.","examples":["You''re going to collapse at 30 seconds."],"segmentIndex":5},{"pattern":"Subordinate Clauses with ''as''","explanation":"Used to introduce time, reason, or comparison in a sentence.","explanationKo":"시간, 이유, 비교 등을 나타내는 부사절을 만들 때 사용합니다.","examples":["as one patient said"],"segmentIndex":80},{"pattern":"Emphasis with ''In no way''","explanation":"Used to stress the negation of a statement, emphasizing that something is not true.","explanationKo":"어떤 것이 참이 아님을 강조하기 위해 사용되는 표현입니다.","examples":["In no way am I suggesting something..."],"segmentIndex":55},{"pattern":"Use of ''be'' in Present Continuous","explanation":"Used to form the present continuous tense, indicating an ongoing action.","explanationKo":"현재 진행 중인 행동을 나타내기 위해 ''be''를 사용합니다.","examples":["You''re about to hold a plank.","You''re going to collapse."],"segmentIndex":1},{"pattern":"Use of ''have been doing'' for Present Perfect Continuous","explanation":"Used to describe an action that started in the past and continues to the present.","explanationKo":"과거에 시작되어 현재까지 지속되는 행동을 나타내는 데 사용합니다.","examples":["I''ve been doing clinical research for over 40 years."],"segmentIndex":47},{"pattern":"Relative Pronouns (''that'')","explanation":"Used to introduce relative clauses that refer to a noun in the main clause.","explanationKo":"주문절의 명사에 대한 추가 정보를 제공하는 관계절을 시작하는 대명사입니다.","examples":["that mental toughness that helps people...","what we''ve learned from George"],"segmentIndex":30},{"pattern":"Subordinate Clauses with ''as'' for Reason","explanation":"Used to indicate a reason or explanation for a main clause.","explanationKo":"주문절의 이유나 설명을 나타내는 부사절로 사용됩니다.","examples":["as one patient said"],"segmentIndex":80},{"pattern":"Use of ''the'' in Noun Phrases","explanation":"Used to specify a particular noun, indicating definiteness.","explanationKo":"특정 명사를 지정하여 명확성을 나타내는 데 사용됩니다.","examples":["the conversations in the room","the level of BDNF"],"segmentIndex":28},{"pattern":"Present Simple for General Statements","explanation":"Used to state facts or general truths without reference to time.","explanationKo":"시간에 관계없이 사실이나 일반 진실을 나타내는 데 사용합니다.","examples":["It''s rooted in biology.","Exercise increases BDNF the most."],"segmentIndex":36},{"pattern":"Negative Sentences with ''not'' and ''am''","explanation":"Used to form negative statements in the first person singular.","explanationKo":"첫 번째 인칭 단수의 부정 문장을 형성하는 데 사용됩니다.","examples":["In no way am I suggesting something..."],"segmentIndex":55}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '{"sections":[{"section":"Introduction","startSegment":0,"endSegment":14,"summary":"The speaker introduces the concept of a plank challenge, describing the physical and mental strain involved, and sets up the story of George Hood''s world record for the longest plank. This establishes the topic of mental toughness and physical endurance.","summaryKo":"말하는 사람은 플랭크 운동의 고통을 묘사하며, 기록을 세운 조지 후드의 이야기를 소개하여 정신적 강함과 신체적 견고함의 주제를 설정합니다.","keyPoints":["Plank challenge as a metaphor for mental toughness","George Hood''s world record of 10 hours","Introduction of the concept of grit"]},{"section":"Main Argument (BDNF and Science)","startSegment":15,"endSegment":30,"summary":"The speaker transitions to explaining brain-derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF), a protein linked to mental resilience and memory, and its connection to physical exercise like planking. This section bridges the plank challenge to scientific research.","summaryKo":"말하는 사람은 정신적 회복력과 기억력에 연결된 뇌 유도 신경성장 인자(BDNF)를 설명하며, 플랭크 운동과의 연결점을 강조합니다.","keyPoints":["BDNF as ''fertilizer for the brain''","Exercise as the most effective way to increase BDNF","Plank as a potential exercise for mental toughness"]},{"section":"Examples and Case Studies","startSegment":31,"endSegment":55,"summary":"The speaker presents real-life examples of individuals (George Hood and Daniel) who demonstrate grit and the role of BDNF in overcoming severe physical and mental challenges, including chronic pain and disability.","summaryKo":"말하는 사람은 조지 후드와 다니엘과 같은 실제 사례를 통해 정신적 강함과 BDNF가 심각한 신체적/정신적 도전을 극복하는 데 어떻게 기여하는지 보여줍니다.","keyPoints":["George Hood''s mental focus during the plank","Daniel''s CRPS pain and his nine-hour plank","BDNF''s role in resilience and pain management"]},{"section":"Study Results and Conclusion","startSegment":56,"endSegment":98,"summary":"The speaker discusses recent research on BDNF and exercise, highlights the need for further studies, and concludes with a call to action for the audience to embrace planking as a tool for building grit and improving quality of life.","summaryKo":"말하는 사람은 BDNF와 운동에 대한 최신 연구를 언급하며, 추가 연구의 필요성을 강조하고, 청중에게 플랭크를 통해 정신적 강함을 키우는 도전을 제안합니다.","keyPoints":["2005 study on mental effort vs. physical exercise","Current study on CRPS and plank therapy","Call to action: ''Do a plank when you need grit''"]}],"signalExpressions":[{"expression":"You''re about to hold a plank. Just 60 seconds.","type":"hook","segmentIndex":1,"role":"청중의 주의를 끌며 운동의 시작을 알리는 개요 제공"},{"expression":"But there was something deeper happening here.","type":"transition","segmentIndex":30,"role":"주제 전환: 플랭크의 물리적 고통에서 정신적 과정으로 이동"},{"expression":"What makes the concept of grit and BDNF so compelling to me","type":"transition","segmentIndex":56,"role":"새로운 주제로 전환: 실생활 사례와 연구 결과 소개"},{"expression":"I''m here to raise awareness so that this relationship between exercise, BDNF, and improving the quality of life may be studied further.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":90,"role":"결론: 연구의 필요성 강조 및 메시지 요약"},{"expression":"Now, I''m going to leave you with the challenge.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":95,"role":"청중에게 행동을 유도하는 마무리 메시지"},{"expression":"Now, think about that for a minute.","type":"emphasis","segmentIndex":54,"role":"청중의 사고를 유도하며 주제를 강조"}]}'::jsonb
)
