ry divine farmer Shen Nong accidentally poisoned himself 72 times.","segmentIndex":1},{"word":"mythical","definition":"occurring in or characteristic of myths or folk tales; imaginary or fictitious","meaningKo":"신화의, 신화적인, 상상 속의","etymology":"Greek ''mythos'' meaning ''story, tale'' + ''-ical''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"myth (story)","suffix":"-ical"},"relatedWords":["myth","mythology","mythological"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/ˈmɪθɪkəl/","contextSentence":"The mythical Chinese inventor of agriculture, highlights tea''s importance to ancient China.","segmentIndex":6},{"word":"archaeological","definition":"relating to the study of human history through excavation of sites and analysis of artifacts","meaningKo":"고고학의, 고고학적인","etymology":"Greek ''arkhaios'' (ancient) + ''logos'' (study)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"archaeo-","root":"log (study)","suffix":"-ical"},"relatedWords":["archaeology","archaeologist","archaic"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/ˌɑːrkiəˈlɒdʒɪkəl/","contextSentence":"Archaeological evidence suggests tea was first cultivated there as early as 6,000 years ago.","segmentIndex":7},{"word":"cultivated","definition":"prepared and used land for growing crops; developed or improved through care","meaningKo":"재배된, 경작된, 교양 있는","etymology":"Latin ''cultivare'' meaning ''to till, tend''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"cultiv (till, grow)","suffix":"-ated"},"relatedWords":["cultivate","cultivation","culture"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"verb (past participle)","phonetic":"/ˈkʌltɪveɪtɪd/","contextSentence":"Tea was first cultivated there as early as 6,000 years ago.","segmentIndex":7},{"word":"porridge","definition":"a soft food made by boiling grain or cereal in water or milk","meaningKo":"죽, 포리지","etymology":"Middle English alteration of ''pottage'' meaning ''soup, stew''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"porr (pot/cook)","suffix":"-idge"},"relatedWords":["pottage","oatmeal","gruel"],"isEssential":false,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/ˈpɒrɪdʒ/","contextSentence":"It was eaten as a vegetable or cooked with grain porridge.","segmentIndex":11},{"word":"moisture","definition":"water or other liquid diffused in a small quantity; dampness","meaningKo":"수분, 습기","etymology":"Old French ''moistour'' from ''moiste'' meaning ''damp''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"moist (damp)","suffix":"-ure"},"relatedWords":["moist","moisten","moisturize"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/ˈmɔɪstʃər/","contextSentence":"When people realized that a combination of heat and moisture could create a complex and varied taste.","segmentIndex":13},{"word":"extravagant","definition":"exceeding what is reasonable or appropriate; elaborate and impressive","meaningKo":"사치스러운, 화려한, 과도한","etymology":"Latin ''extra-'' (outside) + ''vagari'' (to wander)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"extra-","root":"vag (wander)","suffix":"-ant"},"relatedWords":["extravagance","vagrant","vagabond"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/ɪkˈstrævəɡənt/","contextSentence":"They would draw extravagant pictures in the foam of the tea.","segmentIndex":20},{"word":"ritual","definition":"a ceremony or series of acts regularly repeated in a set manner","meaningKo":"의식, 의례, 관례","etymology":"Latin ''ritualis'' from ''ritus'' meaning ''religious ceremony''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"rit (ceremony)","suffix":"-ual"},"relatedWords":["rite","ritualistic","ceremony"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/ˈrɪtʃuəl/","contextSentence":"The Japanese eventually developed their own unique rituals around tea.","segmentIndex":23},{"word":"monopoly","definition":"the exclusive possession or control of the supply of a commodity or service","meaningKo":"독점, 독점권, 전매","etymology":"Greek ''monos'' (single) + ''polein'' (to sell)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"mono-","root":"poly (sell)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["monopolize","monopolistic","oligopoly"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/məˈnɒpəli/","contextSentence":"China still held a virtual monopoly on the world''s tea trees.","segmentIndex":27},{"word":"porcelain","definition":"a hard, white, translucent ceramic material used for making fine pottery","meaningKo":"도자기, 자기","etymology":"Italian ''porcellana'' from ''porcella'' (cowrie shell), due to its resemblance","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"porcell (shell-like)","suffix":"-ain"},"relatedWords":["ceramic","pottery","china"],"isEssential":false,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/ˈpɔːrsəlɪn/","contextSentence":"Making tea one of three essential Chinese export goods, along with porcelain and silk.","segmentIndex":28},{"word":"aristocracy","definition":"the highest class in certain societies, typically comprising people of noble birth","meaningKo":"귀족, 귀족 계급, 상류층","etymology":"Greek ''aristokratia'' from ''aristos'' (best) + ''kratos'' (power, rule)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"aristo (best) + crat (rule)","suffix":"-y"},"relatedWords":["aristocrat","aristocratic","democratic"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/ˌærɪˈstɒkrəsi/","contextSentence":"For making tea popular with the English aristocracy when she married King Charles II in 1661.","segmentIndex":33},{"word":"colonial","definition":"relating to or characteristic of a colony or colonialism","meaningKo":"식민지의, 식민지 시대의","etymology":"Latin ''colonus'' meaning ''farmer, settler'' from ''colere'' (to cultivate)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"colon (settle, cultivate)","suffix":"-ial"},"relatedWords":["colony","colonist","colonize"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/kəˈloʊniəl/","contextSentence":"Great Britain was in the midst of expanding its colonial influence.","segmentIndex":34},{"word":"lucrative","definition":"producing a great deal of profit; very profitable","meaningKo":"수익성이 좋은, 돈벌이가 되는","etymology":"Latin ''lucrativus'' from ''lucrari'' meaning ''to gain profit''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"lucr (profit, gain)","suffix":"-ative"},"relatedWords":["lucre","profitable","gainful"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/ˈluːkrətɪv/","contextSentence":"The tea trade was so lucrative that the world''s fastest sailboat, the Clipper Ship, was born.","segmentIndex":39},{"word":"opium","definition":"a highly addictive narcotic drug obtained from the juice of the opium poppy","meaningKo":"아편","etymology":"Greek ''opion'' meaning ''poppy juice'' from ''opos'' (vegetable juice)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"opi (juice/poppy)","suffix":"-um"},"relatedWords":["opiate","opioid","narcotic"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/ˈoʊpiəm/","contextSentence":"They suggested trading tea for another substance, opium.","segmentIndex":43},{"word":"addicted","definition":"physically and mentally dependent on a particular substance or activity","meaningKo":"중독된, 빠져 있는","etymology":"Latin ''addictus'' meaning ''assigned, devoted'' from ''addicere'' (to devote)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"ad-","root":"dict (say, assign)","suffix":"-ed"},"relatedWords":["addiction","addictive","addict"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/əˈdɪktɪd/","contextSentence":"This triggered a public health problem within China, as people became addicted to the drug.","segmentIndex":44},{"word":"ceded","definition":"gave up power, territory, or rights, especially by treaty","meaningKo":"할양한, 양도한","etymology":"Latin ''cedere'' meaning ''to go, yield, give way''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"ced (go, yield)","suffix":"-ed"},"relatedWords":["cede","concede","precede","secede"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"verb (past tense)","phonetic":"/ˈsiːdɪd/","contextSentence":"The defeated Qing Dynasty ceded the port of Hong Kong to the British.","segmentIndex":49},{"word":"commissioned","definition":"ordered or authorized the production of something; gave an official task","meaningKo":"위임한, 의뢰한, 임명한","etymology":"Latin ''commissio'' from ''committere'' meaning ''to entrust''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"com-","root":"miss (send)","suffix":"-ioned"},"relatedWords":["commission","missionary","mission"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"verb (past tense)","phonetic":"/kəˈmɪʃənd/","contextSentence":"They commissioned botanist Robert Fortune to steal tea from China in a covert operation.","segmentIndex":53},{"word":"perilous","definition":"full of danger or risk; hazardous","meaningKo":"위험한, 위태로운","etymology":"Latin ''periculosus'' from ''periculum'' meaning ''danger, risk''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"peril (danger)","suffix":"-ous"},"relatedWords":["peril","imperil","hazardous"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"adjective","phonetic":"/ˈpɛrɪləs/","contextSentence":"He disguised himself and took a perilous journey through China''s mountainous tea regions.","segmentIndex":54},{"word":"commodity","definition":"a raw material or primary agricultural product that can be bought and sold","meaningKo":"상품, 물자, 원자재","etymology":"Latin ''commoditas'' meaning ''fitness, convenience'' from ''commodus'' (convenient)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"com-","root":"mod (measure, manner)","suffix":"-ity"},"relatedWords":["commodities","accommodate","mode"],"isEssential":true,"partOfSpeech":"noun","phonetic":"/kəˈmɒdɪti/","contextSentence":"Helping drive tea''s rapid growth as an everyday commodity.","segmentIndex":56}]'::jsonb, '[{"pattern":"Past participle phrase as modifier (spent + V-ing)","explanation":"A past participle phrase modifies a noun, adding descriptive information. ''Spent roaming'' describes how the day was occupied.","explanationKo":"과거분사구가 명사를 수식하며 추가 정보를 제공해요. ''spent roaming''은 하루를 어떻게 보냈는지 설명하는 구조로, ''~하며 보낸''이라고 해석해요.","examples":["During a long day spent roaming the forest in search of edible grains and herbs."],"segmentIndex":0},{"pattern":"Before + subject + could + verb (temporal clause)","explanation":"Used to describe an action that almost happened but was prevented. It creates suspense by showing what nearly occurred before an interruption.","explanationKo":"''before + 주어 + could + 동사''는 어떤 일이 일어나기 직전에 다른 일이 개입했음을 나타내요. ''~하기 전에''라는 의미로 긴장감을 만들어요.","examples":["But before the poisons could end his life, a leaf drifted into his mouth."],"segmentIndex":2},{"pattern":"As early as + time expression","explanation":"Used to emphasize that something happened surprisingly long ago. It highlights the ancient or early nature of an event.","explanationKo":"''as early as + 시간 표현''은 어떤 일이 놀라울 정도로 오래전에 일어났음을 강조할 때 사용해요. ''무려 ~이나 이른 시기에''라는 의미예요.","examples":["Tea was first cultivated there as early as 6,000 years ago.","Or 1,500 years before the pharaohs built the Great Pyramids of Giza."],"segmentIndex":7},{"pattern":"Passive voice: was/were + past participle","explanation":"Used when the focus is on the action or result rather than the doer. Common in historical narratives and academic descriptions.","explanationKo":"수동태(be동사 + 과거분사)는 행위자보다 행동이나 결과에 초점을 맞출 때 사용해요. 역사 서술과 학술적 설명에서 자주 쓰이며, ''~되었다''로 해석해요.","examples":["It was eaten as a vegetable or cooked with grain porridge.","Tea was the subject of books and poetry."],"segmentIndex":11},{"pattern":"Would + verb (past habitual / narrative future)","explanation":"Used in narratives to describe repeated actions in the past or to indicate future events from a past perspective.","explanationKo":"''would + 동사원형''은 과거의 반복적 행동을 서술하거나, 과거 시점에서 미래를 이야기할 때 사용해요. ''~하곤 했다'' 또는 ''~하게 될 것이었다''라는 의미예요.","examples":["They would draw extravagant pictures in the foam of the tea."],"segmentIndex":20},{"pattern":"Leading to + noun (result clause with present participle)","explanation":"A participial phrase that indicates a result or consequence of a previous action. It smoothly connects cause and effect.","explanationKo":"''leading to + 명사''는 이전 행동의 결과나 귀결을 나타내는 분사구예요. 원인과 결과를 자연스럽게 연결하며, ''~으로 이어졌다''라는 의미예요.","examples":["Leading to the creation of the Japanese tea ceremony."],"segmentIndex":24},{"pattern":"So + adjective + that + clause (result clause)","explanation":"Used to express cause and effect: the degree of something is so great that it produces a specific result.","explanationKo":"''so + 형용사/부사 + that + 절''은 정도가 너무 커서 특정 결과를 초래함을 표현해요. ''너무 ~해서 …하다''라는 의미의 인과관계 구조예요.","examples":["The tea trade was so lucrative that the world''s fastest sailboat, the Clipper Ship, was born.","Matcha became so popular that a distinct Chinese tea culture emerged."],"segmentIndex":39},{"pattern":"When + clause (temporal transition in narrative)","explanation":"Used to indicate the specific time or condition under which an event occurred. It is a key structure for organizing chronological narratives.","explanationKo":"''when + 절''은 특정 사건이 발생한 시점이나 조건을 나타내요. 시간 순서에 따른 서술을 정리하는 핵심 구조로, ''~했을 때''라는 의미예요.","examples":["When that proved too expensive, they suggested trading tea for another substance.","When the defeated Qing Dynasty ceded the port of Hong Kong to the British."],"segmentIndex":43},{"pattern":"Present participle phrase as adverbial (helping drive...)","explanation":"A present participle phrase used to add information about how or why something happened, functioning as an adverbial modifier.","explanationKo":"현재분사구가 부사적으로 쓰여 어떤 일이 어떻게 또는 왜 일어났는지 부가 설명을 해요. ''~하면서, ~하여''라는 의미로 간결하게 정보를 덧붙여요.","examples":["Helping drive tea''s rapid growth as an everyday commodity.","Making tea one of three essential Chinese export goods."],"segmentIndex":56},{"pattern":"From A to B (range/contrast structure)","explanation":"Used to show the full range or variety of something by presenting two contrasting extremes. It emphasizes diversity.","explanationKo":"''from A to B''는 두 가지 대조적인 극단을 제시하여 범위나 다양성을 보여주는 구조예요. ''A에서 B까지''라는 의미로 다양성을 강조해요.","examples":["And from sugary Turkish Riza tea to salty Tibetan butter tea."],"segmentIndex":58}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"linking","originalText":"search of edible","phonetic":"/sɜːrtʃ_əv_ˈɛdɪbl/","koreanPhonetic":"서처베디블","explanation":"The final /tʃ/ of ''search'' links to the reduced ''of'' (/əv/), and the /v/ then links to the initial vowel /ɛ/ of ''edible,'' creating a smooth chain across three words.","explanationKo":"''search''의 마지막 소리가 약화된 ''of''(/əv/)와 연결되고, /v/가 ''edible''의 첫 모음 /ɛ/과 이어져 세 단어가 매끄럽게 연결돼요.","practiceGuide":"''서치 오브 에디블''이 아니라 ''서처베디블''처럼 끊지 않고 연결해서 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":0},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"poisoned himself","phonetic":"/ˈpɔɪznd_ɪmˈsɛlf/","koreanPhonetic":"포이즌딤셀프","explanation":"The /h/ in ''himself'' is dropped in connected speech, and the /d/ of ''poisoned'' links directly to the /ɪ/ of ''imself.'' This h-dropping is very common with pronouns.","explanationKo":"''himself''의 /h/가 연결 발화에서 탈락하고, ''poisoned''의 /d/가 바로 /ɪ/와 연결돼요. 대명사에서 /h/ 탈락은 매우 흔한 현상이에요.","practiceGuide":"''포이즌드 힘셀프''가 아니라 ''포이즌딤셀프''처럼 /h/를 생략하고 바로 이어서 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":1},{"type":"elision","originalText":"chewed on it","phonetic":"/tʃuːd_ɒnɪt/","koreanPhonetic":"추도닛","explanation":"The /d/ of ''chewed'' softens before ''on,'' and the /n/ of ''on'' links to the /ɪ/ of ''it,'' making the three words sound like one unit.","explanationKo":"''chewed''의 /d/가 ''on'' 앞에서 부드러워지고, ''on''의 /n/이 ''it''의 /ɪ/와 연결되어 세 단어가 하나의 덩어리처럼 들려요.","practiceGuide":"''츄드 온 잇''이 아니라 ''추도닛''처럼 자연스럽게 이어 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":3},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"combination of heat and","phonetic":"/ˌkɒmbɪˈneɪʃən_əv_hiːt_ən/","koreanPhonetic":"컴비네이션어브 히른","explanation":"Both ''of'' and ''and'' are heavily reduced: ''of'' becomes /əv/ or just /ə/, and ''and'' reduces to /ən/ or /n/. Function words are routinely weakened in natural speech.","explanationKo":"''of''와 ''and'' 모두 크게 축약돼요. ''of''는 /ə/로, ''and''는 /ən/ 또는 /n/으로 줄어들어요. 기능어는 자연스러운 발화에서 일상적으로 약화돼요.","practiceGuide":"''컴비네이션 오브 히트 앤드''가 아니라 ''of''를 /어/로, ''and''를 /은/으로 가볍게 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":13},{"type":"linking","originalText":"spread around","phonetic":"/sprɛd_əˈraʊnd/","koreanPhonetic":"스프레더라운드","explanation":"The /d/ at the end of ''spread'' links smoothly to the schwa /ə/ at the start of ''around.'' Consonant-to-vowel linking makes these two words flow as one.","explanationKo":"''spread''의 마지막 /d/가 ''around''의 첫 소리 /ə/와 부드럽게 연결돼요. 자음-모음 연결이 두 단어를 하나처럼 흐르게 해요.","practiceGuide":"''스프레드 어라운드''로 끊지 말고 ''스프레더라운드''처럼 /d/와 /ə/를 이어서 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":36},{"type":"assimilation","originalText":"in earnest","phonetic":"/ɪˈnɜːrnɪst/","koreanPhonetic":"이너니스트","explanation":"The /n/ at the end of ''in'' assimilates with the initial vowel /ɜː/ of ''earnest,'' and the nasal flows directly into the vowel, making both words sound like a single word.","explanationKo":"''in''의 /n/이 ''earnest''의 첫 모음 /ɜː/와 합쳐져 비음이 모음으로 자연스럽게 흘러가며, 두 단어가 하나의 단어처럼 들려요.","practiceGuide":"''인 어니스트''로 끊지 말고 ''이너니스트''처럼 /n/과 /ɜː/를 이어서 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":30},{"type":"elision","originalText":"first opium war","phonetic":"/fɜːs ˈoʊpiəm wɔːr/","koreanPhonetic":"퍼스 오피엄 워","explanation":"The /t/ at the end of ''first'' is elided before the /oʊ/ of ''opium.'' When /st/ clusters precede another consonant or word, the final /t/ is commonly dropped.","explanationKo":"''first''의 마지막 /t/가 ''opium''의 /oʊ/ 앞에서 탈락해요. /st/ 자음군 뒤에 다른 단어가 오면 마지막 /t/가 흔히 생략돼요.","practiceGuide":"''퍼스트 오피엄''에서 /t/를 또렷이 발음하지 말고, ''퍼스 오피엄''처럼 /t/를 생략해 보세요.","segmentIndex":47},{"type":"linking","originalText":"smuggling tea trees and experienced","phonetic":"/ˈsmʌɡlɪŋ tiː triːz_ənd_ɪkˈspɪəriənst/","koreanPhonetic":"스머글링 티 트리전딕스피어리언스트","explanation":"The /z/ of ''trees'' links to the reduced ''and'' (/ənd/ → /ən/), and the /d/ of ''and'' links to the /ɪ/ of ''experienced,'' creating a smooth chain of sounds.","explanationKo":"''trees''의 /z/가 약화된 ''and''와 연결되고, ''and''의 /d/가 ''experienced''의 /ɪ/와 이어져 매끄러운 소리 연쇄가 만들어져요.","practiceGuide":"''트리즈 앤드 익스피어리언스트''가 아니라 연결되는 부분을 끊지 않고 ''트리전딕스피어리언스트''처럼 이어서 발음해 보세요.","segmentIndex":55}]'::jsonb, '{"sections":[{"section":"intro","startSegment":0,"endSegment":4,"summary":"The narrator introduces the legendary origin of tea through the myth of Shen Nong, the divine Chinese farmer who accidentally discovered tea after being poisoned.","summaryKo":"신농씨의 신화를 통해 차의 전설적인 기원을 소개해요. 독에 중독된 후 우연히 차를 발견한 이야기로 청중의 흥미를 끌어요.","keyPoints":["Shen Nong, the divine farmer, was poisoned 72 times","A tea leaf accidentally revived him","This is an ancient legend, not historical fact"]},{"section":"body","startSegment":5,"endSegment":11,"summary":"The narrator transitions from legend to archaeological evidence, explaining that tea was cultivated in China 6,000 years ago and was originally consumed as food, not as a drink.","summaryKo":"전설에서 고고학적 증거로 전환하며, 차가 6,000년 전 중국에서 재배되었고 원래는 음료가 아닌 음식으로 소비되었다고 설명해요.","keyPoints":["Tea cultivation dates back 6,000 years in China","This predates the Great Pyramids by 1,500 years","Tea was originally eaten as a vegetable or with porridge"]},{"section":"body","startSegment":12,"endSegment":21,"summary":"Tea shifted from food to drink 1,500 years ago. The preparation evolved into matcha, and a rich Chinese tea culture emerged with tea becoming a subject of art, poetry, and imperial favor.","summaryKo":"1,500년 전에 차가 음식에서 음료로 바뀌었어요. 준비 방법이 말차로 발전했고, 차가 예술과 시, 황제의 총애의 대상이 되면서 풍부한 중국 차 문화가 형성되었어요.","keyPoints":["Heat and moisture unlocked complex flavors from tea leaves","Matcha became the standard preparation method","Tea culture included art, poetry, and foam art similar to modern latte art"]},{"section":"body","startSegment":22,"endSegment":31,"summary":"Tea spread to Japan in the 9th century, leading to the Japanese tea ceremony. During the Ming Dynasty, loose leaf tea replaced cakes. China maintained a tea monopoly, and Dutch traders brought tea to Europe in the 1600s.","summaryKo":"9세기에 차가 일본에 전해져 다도가 탄생했어요. 명나라 때 잎차가 떡차를 대체했고, 중국은 차 독점권을 유지했으며, 1600년대에 네덜란드 상인들이 차를 유럽에 가져왔어요.","keyPoints":["A Japanese monk brought tea to Japan during the Tang Dynasty","The Ming Dynasty shifted from cake tea to loose leaf tea","China held a monopoly on tea alongside porcelain and silk","Dutch traders brought tea to Europe in large quantities"]},{"section":"body","startSegment":32,"endSegment":41,"summary":"Tea became enormously popular in Europe, particularly England. Its high price and Chinese monopoly fueled intense competition, giving rise to Clipper Ships and a massive global trade.","summaryKo":"차가 유럽, 특히 영국에서 엄청난 인기를 끌었어요. 높은 가격과 중국의 독점이 치열한 경쟁을 부추겨 클리퍼선이 탄생하고 거대한 글로벌 무역이 형성되었어요.","keyPoints":["Queen Catherine of Braganza popularized tea in English aristocracy","Britain''s colonial expansion spread tea culture globally","Tea sold for 10 times the price of coffee in 1700","Clipper Ships were built to race tea to Europe"]},{"section":"body","startSegment":42,"endSegment":51,"summary":"Britain''s tea trade led to the devastating Opium Wars with China. Britain traded opium for tea, triggering addiction and conflict. The defeated Qing Dynasty ceded Hong Kong, weakening China for over a century.","summaryKo":"영국의 차 무역은 중국과의 파괴적인 아편 전쟁으로 이어졌어요. 영국이 차 대신 아편을 교역하면서 중독과 분쟁이 발생했고, 패배한 청나라는 홍콩을 할양하며 1세기 이상 약화되었어요.","keyPoints":["Britain traded opium for Chinese tea when silver became too expensive","Opium caused a public health crisis in China","The first Opium War (1839-1842) resulted in China ceding Hong Kong","The war weakened China''s global standing for over a century"]},{"section":"body","startSegment":52,"endSegment":56,"summary":"The British East India Company sent Robert Fortune on a covert mission to steal tea plants and expertise from China. He smuggled them to Darjeeling, India, breaking China''s monopoly and driving tea''s global spread.","summaryKo":"영국 동인도 회사가 로버트 포춘을 비밀 작전에 보내 중국에서 차나무와 기술을 훔쳐왔어요. 인도 다르질링으로 밀반출하며 중국의 독점을 깨고 차의 세계적 확산을 이끌었어요.","keyPoints":["Robert Fortune disguised himself and infiltrated China''s tea regions","He smuggled tea plants and workers to Darjeeling, India","This broke China''s monopoly and made tea an everyday commodity worldwide"]},{"section":"conclusion","startSegment":57,"endSegment":61,"summary":"Today tea is the world''s second most consumed beverage after water, with an incredible diversity of preparation methods across cultures worldwide.","summaryKo":"오늘날 차는 물 다음으로 세계에서 두 번째로 많이 소비되는 음료이며, 전 세계 문화마다 놀라울 정도로 다양한 준비 방법이 있어요.","keyPoints":["Tea is the second most consumed beverage in the world","Preparation styles range from sugary Turkish tea to salty Tibetan butter tea","There are nearly as many tea traditions as there are cultures"]}],"signalExpressions":[{"expression":"During a long day spent roaming the forest","type":"emphasis","segmentIndex":0,"role":"서사적 묘사로 시작하여 이야기 속으로 청중을 끌어들이는 도입부예요"},{"expression":"And that is how we discovered tea","type":"summary","segmentIndex":4,"role":"전설의 핵심을 요약하며 이야기의 첫 번째 단락을 마무리해요"},{"expression":"Or so an ancient legend goes, at least","type":"transition","segmentIndex":4,"role":"전설에서 사실적 서술로 전환하며, 이야기의 신뢰성에 대한 여지를 남겨요"},{"expression":"Archaeological evidence suggests","type":"transition","segmentIndex":7,"role":"신화에서 과학적 증거로 전환하며 역사적 서술을 시작해요"},{"expression":"Tea only shifted from food to drink 1,500 years ago","type":"transition","segmentIndex":12,"role":"차의 용도 변화라는 중요한 전환점을 알리며 새로운 시대로 넘어가요"},{"expression":"In the 9th century, during the Tang Dynasty","type":"transition","segmentIndex":22,"role":"구체적인 시대와 왕조를 제시하며 일본으로의 차 전파 이야기를 시작해요"},{"expression":"That spread began in earnest around the early 1600s","type":"transition","segmentIndex":30,"role":"차의 세계적 확산이 본격화된 시점을 알리며 유럽 진출 이야기로 전환해요"},{"expression":"At first, Britain paid for all this Chinese tea with silver","type":"transition","segmentIndex":42,"role":"무역 방식의 변화를 소개하며 아편 전쟁으로 이어지는 서술을 시작해요"},{"expression":"This act triggered the first opium war","type":"emphasis","segmentIndex":47,"role":"인과관계를 명확히 하며 전쟁이라는 중대한 사건의 시작을 강조해요"},{"expression":"The British East India Company also wanted","type":"transition","segmentIndex":52,"role":"''also''를 통해 추가적인 영국의 행동을 소개하며 로버트 포춘의 이야기로 전환해요"},{"expression":"Today, tea is the second most consumed beverage","type":"transition","segmentIndex":57,"role":"과거 서술에서 현재로 돌아오며 결론부로 전환해요"}]}'::jsonb
)
