,{"word":"thinking,","start":233.32,"end":233.7},{"word":"I''ve","start":233.98,"end":234.42},{"word":"got","start":234.42,"end":234.62},{"word":"it.","start":234.62,"end":234.92}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":52,"start":235.34,"end":237.62,"textEn":"And then maybe you''ve returned the next day,","textKo":"그런데 다음 날 돌아왔을 때,","words":[{"word":"And","start":235.34,"end":235.9},{"word":"then","start":235.9,"end":236.06},{"word":"maybe","start":236.06,"end":236.54},{"word":"you''ve","start":236.54,"end":236.72},{"word":"returned","start":236.72,"end":237.04},{"word":"the","start":237.04,"end":237.18},{"word":"next","start":237.18,"end":237.4},{"word":"day,","start":237.4,"end":237.62}],"listenDifficulty":4},{"index":53,"start":237.64,"end":240.3,"textEn":"And all those improvements from the day before, they''re lost.","textKo":"전날의 모든 향상이 사라져 버린 적이 있으실 겁니다.","words":[{"word":"and","start":237.64,"end":237.78},{"word":"all","start":237.78,"end":237.96},{"word":"those","start":237.96,"end":238.14},{"word":"improvements","start":238.14,"end":238.7},{"word":"from","start":238.7,"end":238.96},{"word":"the","start":238.96,"end":239.08},{"word":"day","start":239.08,"end":239.2},{"word":"before,","start":239.2,"end":239.56},{"word":"they''re","start":239.62,"end":239.78},{"word":"lost.","start":239.78,"end":240.3}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":54,"start":241.1,"end":245.76,"textEn":"What happened? Well, in the short-term, your brain was able to increase","textKo":"무슨 일이 일어난 걸까요? 단기적으로, 여러분의 뇌는","words":[{"word":"What","start":241.1,"end":241.66},{"word":"happened?","start":241.66,"end":241.98},{"word":"Well,","start":241.98,"end":242.98},{"word":"in","start":243.08,"end":243.14},{"word":"the","start":243.14,"end":243.26},{"word":"short","start":243.26,"end":243.54},{"word":"-term,","start":243.54,"end":243.88},{"word":"your","start":244.2,"end":244.68},{"word":"brain","start":244.68,"end":244.88},{"word":"was","start":244.88,"end":245.04},{"word":"able","start":245.04,"end":245.22},{"word":"to","start":245.22,"end":245.36},{"word":"increase","start":245.36,"end":245.76}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":55,"start":245.76,"end":247.86,"textEn":"The chemical signaling between your neurons.","textKo":"뉴런 사이의 화학 신호를 증가시킬 수 있었습니다.","words":[{"word":"the","start":245.76,"end":245.92},{"word":"chemical","start":245.92,"end":246.32},{"word":"signaling","start":246.32,"end":246.82},{"word":"between","start":246.82,"end":247.18},{"word":"your","start":247.18,"end":247.38},{"word":"neurons.","start":247.38,"end":247.86}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":56,"start":248.06,"end":253.0,"textEn":"But for some reason, those changes did not induce the structural change","textKo":"하지만 어떤 이유에서인지, 그 변화들이 구조적 변화를 유도하지 못했고","words":[{"word":"But","start":248.06,"end":248.5},{"word":"for","start":248.5,"end":248.62},{"word":"some","start":248.62,"end":248.9},{"word":"reason,","start":248.9,"end":249.34},{"word":"those","start":249.34,"end":250.06},{"word":"changes","start":250.06,"end":250.58},{"word":"did","start":250.58,"end":250.92},{"word":"not","start":250.92,"end":251.14},{"word":"induce","start":251.14,"end":251.56},{"word":"the","start":251.56,"end":251.86},{"word":"structural","start":251.86,"end":252.36},{"word":"change","start":252.36,"end":253.0}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":57,"start":253.52,"end":255.92,"textEn":"That are necessary to support long-term memory.","textKo":"장기 기억을 지원하기 위해 필요한 변화가 일어나지 않은 것입니다.","words":[{"word":"that","start":253.34,"end":253.64},{"word":"are","start":253.64,"end":253.76},{"word":"necessary","start":253.76,"end":254.3},{"word":"to","start":254.3,"end":254.8},{"word":"support","start":254.8,"end":255.1},{"word":"long","start":255.1,"end":255.38},{"word":"-term","start":255.38,"end":255.58},{"word":"memory.","start":255.58,"end":255.92}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":58,"start":257.12,"end":260.0,"textEn":"Remember that long-term memories take time,","textKo":"장기 기억에는 시간이 걸린다는 것을 기억하세요.","words":[{"word":"Remember","start":257.12,"end":257.72},{"word":"that","start":257.72,"end":258.26},{"word":"long","start":258.26,"end":258.68},{"word":"-term","start":258.68,"end":258.88},{"word":"memories","start":258.88,"end":259.16},{"word":"take","start":259.16,"end":259.46},{"word":"time,","start":259.46,"end":260.0}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":59,"start":260.56,"end":263.24,"textEn":"And what you see in the short-term does not reflect learning.","textKo":"그리고 단기적으로 보이는 것이 학습을 반영하는 것은 아닙니다.","words":[{"word":"and","start":260.4,"end":260.7},{"word":"what","start":260.7,"end":260.84},{"word":"you","start":260.84,"end":260.96},{"word":"see","start":260.96,"end":261.18},{"word":"in","start":261.18,"end":261.32},{"word":"the","start":261.32,"end":261.42},{"word":"short","start":261.42,"end":261.68},{"word":"-term","start":261.68,"end":261.9},{"word":"does","start":261.9,"end":262.1},{"word":"not","start":262.1,"end":262.4},{"word":"reflect","start":262.4,"end":262.78},{"word":"learning.","start":262.78,"end":263.24}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":60,"start":263.56,"end":267.58,"textEn":"It''s these physical changes that are now going to support long-term memories,","textKo":"이러한 물리적 변화가 바로 장기 기억을 지원하게 될 것이고,","words":[{"word":"It''s","start":263.56,"end":264.16},{"word":"these","start":264.16,"end":264.36},{"word":"physical","start":264.36,"end":264.82},{"word":"changes","start":264.82,"end":265.28},{"word":"that","start":265.28,"end":265.54},{"word":"are","start":265.54,"end":265.64},{"word":"now","start":265.64,"end":265.78},{"word":"going","start":265.78,"end":265.94},{"word":"to","start":265.94,"end":266.06},{"word":"support","start":266.06,"end":266.5},{"word":"long","start":266.5,"end":267.04},{"word":"-term","start":267.04,"end":267.26},{"word":"memories,","start":267.26,"end":267.58}],"listenDifficulty":4},{"index":61,"start":267.58,"end":271.28,"textEn":"And chemical changes that support short-term memories.","textKo":"화학적 변화는 단기 기억을 지원합니다.","words":[{"word":"and","start":267.58,"end":267.78},{"word":"chemical","start":267.78,"end":268.16},{"word":"changes","start":268.16,"end":268.64},{"word":"that","start":268.64,"end":269.26},{"word":"support","start":269.26,"end":269.74},{"word":"short","start":269.74,"end":270.62},{"word":"-term","start":270.62,"end":270.84},{"word":"memories.","start":270.84,"end":271.28}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":62,"start":272.66,"end":276.66,"textEn":"Structural changes also can lead to integrated networks of brain regions","textKo":"구조적 변화는 또한 학습을 지원하기 위해 함께 기능하는","words":[{"word":"Structural","start":272.66,"end":273.26},{"word":"changes","start":273.26,"end":273.6},{"word":"also","start":273.6,"end":274.0},{"word":"can","start":274.0,"end":274.2},{"word":"lead","start":274.2,"end":274.36},{"word":"to","start":274.36,"end":274.5},{"word":"integrated","start":274.5,"end":274.98},{"word":"networks","start":274.98,"end":275.66},{"word":"of","start":275.66,"end":275.96},{"word":"brain","start":275.96,"end":276.22},{"word":"regions","start":276.22,"end":276.66}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":63,"start":276.66,"end":281.48,"textEn":"That function together to support learning. And they can also lead to certain brain regions","textKo":"뇌 영역의 통합된 네트워크로 이어질 수 있습니다. 그리고 특정 행동에 중요한","words":[{"word":"that","start":276.66,"end":276.84},{"word":"function","start":276.84,"end":277.26},{"word":"together","start":277.26,"end":277.68},{"word":"to","start":277.68,"end":277.88},{"word":"support","start":277.88,"end":278.18},{"word":"learning.","start":278.18,"end":278.56},{"word":"And","start":278.82,"end":279.42},{"word":"they","start":279.42,"end":279.52},{"word":"can","start":279.52,"end":279.64},{"word":"also","start":279.64,"end":279.98},{"word":"lead","start":279.98,"end":280.26},{"word":"to","start":280.26,"end":280.52},{"word":"certain","start":280.52,"end":280.92},{"word":"brain","start":280.92,"end":281.18},{"word":"regions","start":281.18,"end":281.48}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":64,"start":281.48,"end":283.5,"textEn":"That are important for very specific behaviors","textKo":"특정 뇌 영역이","words":[{"word":"that","start":281.48,"end":281.62},{"word":"are","start":281.62,"end":281.72},{"word":"important","start":281.72,"end":282.04},{"word":"for","start":282.04,"end":282.22},{"word":"very","start":282.22,"end":282.4},{"word":"specific","start":282.4,"end":282.84},{"word":"behaviors","start":282.84,"end":283.5}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":65,"start":283.5,"end":286.08,"textEn":"To change their structure or to enlarge.","textKo":"구조를 변경하거나 확대되도록 할 수도 있습니다.","words":[{"word":"to","start":283.5,"end":284.26},{"word":"change","start":284.26,"end":284.5},{"word":"their","start":284.5,"end":284.64},{"word":"structure","start":284.64,"end":285.04},{"word":"or","start":285.04,"end":285.24},{"word":"to","start":285.24,"end":285.38},{"word":"enlarge.","start":285.38,"end":286.08}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":66,"start":286.34,"end":288.38,"textEn":"And so here are some examples of that.","textKo":"여기 몇 가지 예가 있습니다.","words":[{"word":"And","start":286.34,"end":286.82},{"word":"so","start":286.82,"end":287.0},{"word":"here","start":287.0,"end":287.18},{"word":"are","start":287.18,"end":287.26},{"word":"some","start":287.26,"end":287.4},{"word":"examples","start":287.4,"end":287.86},{"word":"of","start":287.86,"end":288.08},{"word":"that.","start":288.08,"end":288.38}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":67,"start":288.8,"end":294.2,"textEn":"So people who read Braille, they have larger hand sensory areas in their brain","textKo":"점자를 읽는 사람들은 뇌에서 손 감각 영역이 더 큽니다.","words":[{"word":"So","start":288.8,"end":289.34},{"word":"people","start":289.34,"end":289.66},{"word":"who","start":289.66,"end":289.84},{"word":"read","start":289.84,"end":290.14},{"word":"Braille,","start":290.14,"end":290.7},{"word":"they","start":290.86,"end":291.24},{"word":"have","start":291.24,"end":291.38},{"word":"larger","start":291.38,"end":291.86},{"word":"hand","start":291.86,"end":292.42},{"word":"sensory","start":292.42,"end":292.98},{"word":"areas","start":292.98,"end":293.48},{"word":"in","start":293.48,"end":293.66},{"word":"their","start":293.66,"end":293.8},{"word":"brain","start":293.8,"end":294.2}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":68,"start":294.2,"end":298.98,"textEn":"Than those of us who don''t. Your dominant hand motor region,","textKo":"읽지 않는 우리보다요. 여러분의 우세한 손의 운동 영역은,","words":[{"word":"than","start":294.2,"end":294.52},{"word":"those","start":294.52,"end":294.74},{"word":"of","start":294.74,"end":294.9},{"word":"us","start":294.9,"end":295.04},{"word":"who","start":295.04,"end":295.2},{"word":"don''t.","start":295.2,"end":295.7},{"word":"Your","start":296.7,"end":297.26},{"word":"dominant","start":297.26,"end":297.82},{"word":"hand","start":297.82,"end":298.18},{"word":"motor","start":298.18,"end":298.52},{"word":"region,","start":298.52,"end":298.98}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":69,"start":299.24,"end":303.8,"textEn":"Which is on the left side of your brain, if you''re right-handed, is larger than the other side.","textKo":"오른손잡이라면 뇌의 왼쪽에 있는데, 반대쪽보다 더 큽니다.","words":[{"word":"which","start":299.24,"end":299.36},{"word":"is","start":299.36,"end":299.46},{"word":"on","start":299.46,"end":299.58},{"word":"the","start":299.58,"end":299.7},{"word":"left","start":299.7,"end":299.96},{"word":"side","start":299.96,"end":300.18},{"word":"of","start":300.18,"end":300.32},{"word":"your","start":300.32,"end":300.44},{"word":"brain,","start":300.44,"end":300.86},{"word":"if","start":300.98,"end":301.14},{"word":"you''re","start":301.14,"end":301.28},{"word":"right","start":301.28,"end":301.5},{"word":"-handed,","start":301.5,"end":301.94},{"word":"is","start":302.16,"end":302.3},{"word":"larger","start":302.3,"end":302.74},{"word":"than","start":302.74,"end":303.08},{"word":"the","start":303.08,"end":303.22},{"word":"other","start":303.22,"end":303.4},{"word":"side.","start":303.4,"end":303.8}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":70,"start":304.28,"end":307.54,"textEn":"And research shows that London taxicab drivers","textKo":"그리고 연구에 따르면 런던 택시 운전사들은","words":[{"word":"And","start":304.28,"end":304.84},{"word":"research","start":304.84,"end":305.18},{"word":"shows","start":305.18,"end":305.6},{"word":"that","start":305.6,"end":305.94},{"word":"London","start":305.94,"end":306.36},{"word":"taxicab","start":306.36,"end":307.14},{"word":"drivers","start":307.14,"end":307.54}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":71,"start":307.54,"end":310.16,"textEn":"Who actually have to memorize a map of London","textKo":"택시 면허를 따기 위해 실제로 런던 지도를 외워야 하는데,","words":[{"word":"who","start":307.54,"end":307.82},{"word":"actually","start":307.82,"end":308.16},{"word":"have","start":308.16,"end":308.38},{"word":"to","start":308.38,"end":308.54},{"word":"memorize","start":308.54,"end":309.02},{"word":"a","start":309.02,"end":309.48},{"word":"map","start":309.48,"end":309.7},{"word":"of","start":309.7,"end":309.88},{"word":"London","start":309.88,"end":310.16}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":72,"start":310.16,"end":316.22,"textEn":"To get their taxicab license, they have larger brain regions devoted to spatial or mapping memories.","textKo":"공간적 또는 지도 기억에 할당된 뇌 영역이 더 큽니다.","words":[{"word":"to","start":310.16,"end":310.4},{"word":"get","start":310.4,"end":310.52},{"word":"their","start":310.52,"end":310.66},{"word":"taxicab","start":310.66,"end":311.22},{"word":"license,","start":311.22,"end":311.64},{"word":"they","start":312.02,"end":312.64},{"word":"have","start":312.64,"end":312.8},{"word":"larger","start":312.8,"end":313.18},{"word":"brain","start":313.18,"end":313.48},{"word":"regions","start":313.48,"end":313.86},{"word":"devoted","start":313.86,"end":314.2},{"word":"to","start":314.2,"end":314.42},{"word":"spatial","start":314.42,"end":314.94},{"word":"or","start":314.94,"end":315.32},{"word":"mapping","start":315.32,"end":315.74},{"word":"memories.","start":315.74,"end":316.22}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":73,"start":317.44,"end":320.72,"textEn":"Now, the last way that your brain can change to support learning","textKo":"이제, 여러분의 뇌가 학습을 지원하기 위해 변할 수 있는 마지막 방법은","words":[{"word":"Now,","start":317.44,"end":318.0},{"word":"the","start":318.08,"end":318.16},{"word":"last","start":318.16,"end":318.44},{"word":"way","start":318.44,"end":318.64},{"word":"that","start":318.64,"end":318.78},{"word":"your","start":318.78,"end":318.9},{"word":"brain","start":318.9,"end":319.12},{"word":"can","start":319.12,"end":319.36},{"word":"change","start":319.36,"end":319.8},{"word":"to","start":319.8,"end":320.02},{"word":"support","start":320.02,"end":320.38},{"word":"learning","start":320.38,"end":320.72}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":74,"start":320.72,"end":325.26,"textEn":"Is by altering its function. As you use a brain region,","textKo":"기능을 변경하는 것입니다. 뇌 영역을 사용할수록,","words":[{"word":"is","start":320.72,"end":320.9},{"word":"by","start":320.9,"end":321.02},{"word":"altering","start":321.02,"end":321.4},{"word":"its","start":321.4,"end":321.56},{"word":"function.","start":321.56,"end":321.98},{"word":"As","start":323.48,"end":324.08},{"word":"you","start":324.08,"end":324.2},{"word":"use","start":324.2,"end":324.48},{"word":"a","start":324.48,"end":324.6},{"word":"brain","start":324.6,"end":324.84},{"word":"region,","start":324.84,"end":325.26}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":75,"start":325.4,"end":328.62,"textEn":"It becomes more and more excitable and easy to use again.","textKo":"그 영역은 점점 더 흥분하기 쉬워지고 다시 사용하기 쉬워집니다.","words":[{"word":"it","start":325.4,"end":325.5},{"word":"becomes","start":325.5,"end":325.78},{"word":"more","start":325.78,"end":326.12},{"word":"and","start":326.12,"end":326.26},{"word":"more","start":326.26,"end":326.4},{"word":"excitable","start":326.4,"end":327.12},{"word":"and","start":327.12,"end":327.42},{"word":"easy","start":327.42,"end":327.76},{"word":"to","start":327.76,"end":327.98},{"word":"use","start":327.98,"end":328.26},{"word":"again.","start":328.26,"end":328.62}],"listenDifficulty":4},{"index":76,"start":329.12,"end":332.64,"textEn":"And as your brain has these areas that increase their excitability,","textKo":"그리고 뇌의 이러한 영역들이 흥분성을 증가시키면,","words":[{"word":"And","start":329.12,"end":329.56},{"word":"as","start":329.56,"end":329.72},{"word":"your","start":329.72,"end":329.9},{"word":"brain","start":329.9,"end":330.28},{"word":"has","start":330.28,"end":330.6},{"word":"these","start":330.6,"end":330.8},{"word":"areas","start":330.8,"end":331.18},{"word":"that","start":331.18,"end":331.36},{"word":"increase","start":331.36,"end":331.76},{"word":"their","start":331.76,"end":331.98},{"word":"excitability,","start":331.98,"end":332.64}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":77,"start":332.9,"end":335.16,"textEn":"The brain shifts how and when they''re activated.","textKo":"뇌는 그것들이 언제 어떻게 활성화되는지를 전환합니다.","words":[{"word":"the","start":332.9,"end":332.98},{"word":"brain","start":332.98,"end":333.14},{"word":"shifts","start":333.14,"end":333.42},{"word":"how","start":333.42,"end":333.76},{"word":"and","start":333.76,"end":334.12},{"word":"when","start":334.12,"end":334.4},{"word":"they''re","start":334.4,"end":334.58},{"word":"activated.","start":334.58,"end":335.16}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":78,"start":335.84,"end":339.18,"textEn":"With learning, we see that whole networks of brain activity","textKo":"학습을 통해, 뇌 활동의 전체 네트워크가","words":[{"word":"With","start":335.84,"end":336.44},{"word":"learning,","start":336.44,"end":336.86},{"word":"we","start":337.02,"end":337.1},{"word":"see","start":337.1,"end":337.26},{"word":"that","start":337.26,"end":337.42},{"word":"whole","start":337.42,"end":337.72},{"word":"networks","start":337.72,"end":338.34},{"word":"of","start":338.34,"end":338.62},{"word":"brain","start":338.62,"end":338.82},{"word":"activity","start":338.82,"end":339.18}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":79,"start":339.18,"end":345.2,"textEn":"Are shifting and changing. So neuroplasticity is supported by chemical,","textKo":"이동하고 변화하는 것을 볼 수 있습니다. 신경가소성은 화학적,","words":[{"word":"are","start":339.18,"end":339.46},{"word":"shifting","start":339.46,"end":339.94},{"word":"and","start":339.94,"end":340.28},{"word":"changing.","start":340.28,"end":340.86},{"word":"So","start":342.38,"end":342.98},{"word":"neuroplasticity","start":342.98,"end":343.58},{"word":"is","start":343.58,"end":343.74},{"word":"supported","start":343.74,"end":344.18},{"word":"by","start":344.18,"end":344.5},{"word":"chemical,","start":344.5,"end":345.2}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":80,"start":345.76,"end":347.98,"textEn":"By structural, and by functional changes.","textKo":"구조적, 그리고 기능적 변화에 의해 지원됩니다.","words":[{"word":"by","start":345.76,"end":346.04},{"word":"structural,","start":346.04,"end":346.52},{"word":"and","start":346.56,"end":346.8},{"word":"by","start":346.8,"end":346.94},{"word":"functional","start":346.94,"end":347.48},{"word":"changes.","start":347.48,"end":347.98}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":81,"start":347.98,"end":350.76,"textEn":"And these are happening across the whole brain.","textKo":"그리고 이것은 뇌 전체에 걸쳐 일어나고 있습니다.","words":[{"word":"And","start":347.98,"end":348.86},{"word":"these","start":348.86,"end":349.28},{"word":"are","start":349.28,"end":349.38},{"word":"happening","start":349.38,"end":349.68},{"word":"across","start":349.68,"end":349.98},{"word":"the","start":349.98,"end":350.2},{"word":"whole","start":350.2,"end":350.4},{"word":"brain.","start":350.4,"end":350.76}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":82,"start":351.12,"end":353.64,"textEn":"They can occur in isolation from one another,","textKo":"서로 독립적으로 일어날 수 있지만,","words":[{"word":"They","start":351.12,"end":351.62},{"word":"can","start":351.62,"end":351.8},{"word":"occur","start":351.8,"end":352.06},{"word":"in","start":352.06,"end":352.18},{"word":"isolation","start":352.18,"end":352.7},{"word":"from","start":352.7,"end":353.08},{"word":"one","start":353.08,"end":353.26},{"word":"another,","start":353.26,"end":353.64}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":83,"start":353.72,"end":356.22,"textEn":"But most often they take place in concert.","textKo":"대부분의 경우 함께 일어납니다.","words":[{"word":"but","start":353.72,"end":354.0},{"word":"most","start":354.0,"end":354.4},{"word":"often","start":354.4,"end":354.76},{"word":"they","start":354.76,"end":355.08},{"word":"take","start":355.08,"end":355.28},{"word":"place","start":355.28,"end":355.54},{"word":"in","start":355.54,"end":355.74},{"word":"concert.","start":355.74,"end":356.22}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":84,"start":357.0,"end":361.8,"textEn":"Together they support learning. And they''re taking place all the time.","textKo":"함께 학습을 지원합니다. 그리고 이것은 항상 일어나고 있습니다.","words":[{"word":"Together","start":357.0,"end":357.64},{"word":"they","start":357.64,"end":357.88},{"word":"support","start":357.88,"end":358.32},{"word":"learning.","start":358.32,"end":358.84},{"word":"And","start":359.08,"end":359.64},{"word":"they''re","start":359.64,"end":359.8},{"word":"taking","start":359.8,"end":360.1},{"word":"place","start":360.1,"end":360.7},{"word":"all","start":360.7,"end":361.3},{"word":"the","start":361.3,"end":361.46},{"word":"time.","start":361.46,"end":361.8}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":85,"start":363.56,"end":368.18,"textEn":"So I''ve just told you really how awesomely neuroplastic your brain is.","textKo":"방금 여러분의 뇌가 얼마나 놀랍도록 신경가소적인지 말씀드렸습니다.","words":[{"word":"So","start":363.56,"end":364.2},{"word":"I''ve","start":364.2,"end":364.34},{"word":"just","start":364.34,"end":364.48},{"word":"told","start":364.48,"end":364.8},{"word":"you","start":364.8,"end":365.04},{"word":"really","start":365.04,"end":365.42},{"word":"how","start":365.42,"end":365.62},{"word":"awesomely","start":365.62,"end":366.44},{"word":"neuroplastic","start":366.44,"end":367.12},{"word":"your","start":367.12,"end":367.46},{"word":"brain","start":367.46,"end":367.78},{"word":"is.","start":367.78,"end":368.18}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":86,"start":368.44,"end":371.52,"textEn":"So why can''t you learn anything you choose to with ease?","textKo":"그렇다면 왜 여러분은 원하는 것을 쉽게 배울 수 없을까요?","words":[{"word":"So","start":368.44,"end":369.08},{"word":"why","start":369.08,"end":369.54},{"word":"can''t","start":369.54,"end":369.82},{"word":"you","start":369.82,"end":369.92},{"word":"learn","start":369.92,"end":370.12},{"word":"anything","start":370.12,"end":370.42},{"word":"you","start":370.42,"end":370.62},{"word":"choose","start":370.62,"end":370.88},{"word":"to","start":370.88,"end":371.06},{"word":"with","start":371.06,"end":371.24},{"word":"ease?","start":371.24,"end":371.52}],"listenDifficulty":4},{"index":87,"start":372.6,"end":375.42,"textEn":"Why do our kids sometimes fail in school?","textKo":"왜 우리 아이들은 때때로 학교에서 실패할까요?","words":[{"word":"Why","start":372.6,"end":373.24},{"word":"do","start":373.24,"end":373.34},{"word":"our","start":373.34,"end":373.48},{"word":"kids","start":373.48,"end":373.86},{"word":"sometimes","start":373.86,"end":374.46},{"word":"fail","start":374.46,"end":374.88},{"word":"in","start":374.88,"end":375.08},{"word":"school?","start":375.08,"end":375.42}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":88,"start":376.56,"end":379.44,"textEn":"Why, as we age, do we tend to forget things?","textKo":"왜 나이가 들면서 우리는 것들을 잊어버리는 경향이 있을까요?","words":[{"word":"Why,","start":376.56,"end":377.12},{"word":"as","start":377.12,"end":377.26},{"word":"we","start":377.26,"end":377.42},{"word":"age,","start":377.42,"end":377.8},{"word":"do","start":377.94,"end":378.0},{"word":"we","start":378.0,"end":378.12},{"word":"tend","start":378.12,"end":378.34},{"word":"to","start":378.34,"end":378.5},{"word":"forget","start":378.5,"end":378.8},{"word":"things?","start":378.8,"end":379.44}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":89,"start":380.24,"end":383.36,"textEn":"And why don''t people fully recover from brain damage?","textKo":"그리고 왜 사람들은 뇌 손상에서 완전히 회복하지 못할까요?","words":[{"word":"And","start":380.24,"end":380.8},{"word":"why","start":380.8,"end":381.2},{"word":"don''t","start":381.2,"end":381.44},{"word":"people","start":381.44,"end":381.7},{"word":"fully","start":381.7,"end":382.04},{"word":"recover","start":382.04,"end":382.4},{"word":"from","start":382.4,"end":382.72},{"word":"brain","start":382.72,"end":382.92},{"word":"damage?","start":382.92,"end":383.36}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":90,"start":384.04,"end":388.92,"textEn":"That is, what is it that limits and facilitates neuroplasticity?","textKo":"즉, 신경가소성을 제한하고 촉진하는 것은 무엇일까요?","words":[{"word":"That","start":384.04,"end":384.6},{"word":"is,","start":384.6,"end":384.76},{"word":"what","start":384.9,"end":385.06},{"word":"is","start":385.06,"end":385.22},{"word":"it","start":385.22,"end":385.36},{"word":"that","start":385.36,"end":385.54},{"word":"limits","start":385.54,"end":386.12},{"word":"and","start":386.12,"end":386.58},{"word":"facilitates","start":386.58,"end":387.7},{"word":"neuroplasticity?","start":387.7,"end":388.92}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":91,"start":389.28,"end":394.52,"textEn":"And so this is what I study. I study it specifically how it relates to recovery from stroke.","textKo":"이것이 제가 연구하는 것입니다. 특히 뇌졸중 회복과 관련하여 연구하고 있습니다.","words":[{"word":"And","start":389.28,"end":389.74},{"word":"so","start":389.74,"end":389.9},{"word":"this","start":389.9,"end":390.2},{"word":"is","start":390.2,"end":390.32},{"word":"what","start":390.32,"end":390.46},{"word":"I","start":390.46,"end":390.6},{"word":"study.","start":390.6,"end":391.04},{"word":"I","start":391.22,"end":391.34},{"word":"study","start":391.34,"end":391.62},{"word":"it","start":391.62,"end":391.74},{"word":"specifically","start":391.74,"end":392.26},{"word":"how","start":392.26,"end":392.52},{"word":"it","start":392.52,"end":392.66},{"word":"relates","start":392.66,"end":392.98},{"word":"to","start":392.98,"end":393.14},{"word":"recovery","start":393.14,"end":393.56},{"word":"from","start":393.56,"end":394.02},{"word":"stroke.","start":394.02,"end":394.52}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":92,"start":395.28,"end":399.18,"textEn":"So recently, stroke dropped from being the third leading cause of death","textKo":"최근에 뇌졸중은 미국에서 세 번째 사망 원인에서","words":[{"word":"So","start":395.28,"end":395.84},{"word":"recently,","start":395.84,"end":396.28},{"word":"stroke","start":396.28,"end":396.7},{"word":"dropped","start":396.7,"end":397.12},{"word":"from","start":397.12,"end":397.4},{"word":"being","start":397.4,"end":397.6},{"word":"the","start":397.6,"end":397.84},{"word":"third","start":397.84,"end":398.16},{"word":"leading","start":398.16,"end":398.48},{"word":"cause","start":398.48,"end":398.8},{"word":"of","start":398.8,"end":398.98},{"word":"death","start":398.98,"end":399.18}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":93,"start":399.18,"end":401.66,"textEn":"In the United States to be the fourth leading cause of death.","textKo":"네 번째 사망 원인으로 떨어졌습니다.","words":[{"word":"in","start":399.18,"end":399.36},{"word":"the","start":399.36,"end":399.46},{"word":"United","start":399.46,"end":399.66},{"word":"States","start":399.66,"end":400.02},{"word":"to","start":400.02,"end":400.16},{"word":"be","start":400.16,"end":400.24},{"word":"the","start":400.24,"end":400.38},{"word":"fourth","start":400.38,"end":400.72},{"word":"leading","start":400.72,"end":400.96},{"word":"cause","start":400.96,"end":401.24},{"word":"of","start":401.24,"end":401.38},{"word":"death.","start":401.38,"end":401.66}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":94,"start":401.66,"end":407.72,"textEn":"Great news, right? Well, it actually turns out that the numbers of people having a stroke","textKo":"좋은 소식이죠, 그렇죠? 사실, 뇌졸중을 겪는 사람의 수는","words":[{"word":"Great","start":401.66,"end":402.88},{"word":"news,","start":402.88,"end":403.2},{"word":"right?","start":403.38,"end":403.52},{"word":"Well,","start":404.46,"end":405.02},{"word":"it","start":405.08,"end":405.14},{"word":"actually","start":405.14,"end":405.32},{"word":"turns","start":405.32,"end":405.64},{"word":"out","start":405.64,"end":405.96},{"word":"that","start":405.96,"end":406.12},{"word":"the","start":406.12,"end":406.3},