tial":true,"segmentIndex":8,"contextSentence":"And yet, through my manner of speaking,"},{"word":"brilliant","phonetic":"/ˈbrɪl.jənt/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"exceptionally clever or talented; outstanding","meaningKo":"훌륭한, 뛰어난","etymology":"From French ''brillant'', from Italian ''brillare'' (to shine)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"brill (shine)","suffix":"-ant (characterized by)"},"relatedWords":["brilliance","brilliantly"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":9,"contextSentence":"Like what I am saying is brilliant."},{"word":"inspirational","phonetic":"/ˌɪn.spɪˈreɪ.ʃən.əl/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"providing encouragement or motivation","meaningKo":"영감을 주는","etymology":"From Latin ''inspirare'' (to breathe into)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"in- (into)","root":"spir (breathe)","suffix":"-ational (relating to)"},"relatedWords":["inspire","inspiration","inspiring"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":6,"contextSentence":"Nothing smart. Nothing inspirational."},{"word":"remotely","phonetic":"/rɪˈmoʊt.li/","partOfSpeech":"adverb","definition":"to even the slightest degree; in the least","meaningKo":"조금이라도, 약간이라도","etymology":"From Latin ''remotus'' (removed, distant)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"re- (back)","root":"mot (move)","suffix":"-ly (in the manner of)"},"relatedWords":["remote","remoteness"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":7,"contextSentence":"Nothing even remotely researched at all."},{"word":"whatsoever","phonetic":"/ˌwɒt.soʊˈev.ər/","partOfSpeech":"adverb","definition":"at all; used for emphasis after a negative statement","meaningKo":"전혀, 조금도 (강조)","etymology":"From Middle English ''what so ever'', a compound emphatic form","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"what + so + ever","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["whatever","whoever","however"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":7,"contextSentence":"I have absolutely nothing to say whatsoever."},{"word":"anecdote","phonetic":"/ˈæn.ɪk.doʊt/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"a short, interesting or amusing story about a real incident or person","meaningKo":"일화, 짧은 이야기","etymology":"From Greek ''anekdota'' (things unpublished)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"an- (not)","root":"ekdotos (published)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["anecdotal","anecdotally"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":16,"contextSentence":"I''m going to react to that and act like I''m telling you a personal anecdote."},{"word":"endear","phonetic":"/ɪnˈdɪr/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"to cause someone to be liked or loved","meaningKo":"사랑받게 하다, 호감을 사다","etymology":"From ''en-'' (make) + ''dear'' (beloved)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"en- (cause to be)","root":"dear (beloved)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["endearing","endearment","dear"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":17,"contextSentence":"Something to endear myself a little bit."},{"word":"broader","phonetic":"/ˈbrɔː.dər/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"wider or more extensive in scope","meaningKo":"더 넓은, 더 광범위한","etymology":"From Old English ''brad'' (broad, wide)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"broad (wide)","suffix":"-er (comparative)"},"relatedWords":["broad","broadly","broaden"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":20,"contextSentence":"And now, I''m going to bring it to a broader point."},{"word":"intellectual","phonetic":"/ˌɪn.təˈlek.tʃu.əl/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"relating to or involving the intellect; requiring deep thinking","meaningKo":"지적인, 지성적인","etymology":"From Latin ''intellectualis'', from ''intellectus'' (understanding)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"intel- (between)","root":"lect (choose, read)","suffix":"-ual (relating to)"},"relatedWords":["intellect","intellectually","intelligence"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":21,"contextSentence":"I''m going to make it intellectual."},{"word":"imparted","phonetic":"/ɪmˈpɑːr.tɪd/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"communicated or made known; shared (information or knowledge)","meaningKo":"전달된, 전해진","etymology":"From Latin ''impartire'' (to share, give a part of)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"im- (into)","root":"part (part, share)","suffix":"-ed (past tense)"},"relatedWords":["impart","impartial","part"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":29,"contextSentence":"Interesting facts imparted thus far in said talk."},{"word":"staggering","phonetic":"/ˈstæɡ.ər.ɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"extremely surprising or shocking; astonishing","meaningKo":"놀라운, 엄청난","etymology":"From Old Norse ''stakra'' (to push, stagger)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"stagger (totter)","suffix":"-ing (causing)"},"relatedWords":["stagger","staggeringly"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":38,"contextSentence":"Staggering. These are real numbers, all of them."},{"word":"majority","phonetic":"/məˈdʒɔːr.ə.ti/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"the greater number or part; more than half","meaningKo":"다수, 대부분","etymology":"From Latin ''majoritas'', from ''major'' (greater)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"major (greater)","suffix":"-ity (state of)"},"relatedWords":["major","minority","majorly"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":40,"contextSentence":"The majority far exceeds the minority."},{"word":"irrelevant","phonetic":"/ɪˈrel.ə.vənt/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"not connected with or relevant to something","meaningKo":"관련 없는, 상관없는","etymology":"From Latin ''in-'' (not) + ''relevare'' (to raise up, relieve)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"ir- (not)","root":"relev (raise, relate)","suffix":"-ant (characterized by)"},"relatedWords":["relevant","relevance","irrelevance"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":42,"contextSentence":"It shows similarly irrelevant data."},{"word":"floundering","phonetic":"/ˈflaʊn.dər.ɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"struggling or stumbling helplessly; having difficulty","meaningKo":"허둥대는, 갈팡질팡하는","etymology":"Possibly a blend of ''flounder'' (a fish) and ''blunder''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"flounder (struggle)","suffix":"-ing (present participle)"},"relatedWords":["flounder","founder"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":46,"contextSentence":"I''m floundering, panicking, I''ve got nothing."},{"word":"phony","phonetic":"/ˈfoʊ.ni/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"a person or thing that is not genuine; a fraud","meaningKo":"사기꾼, 가짜","etymology":"Origin uncertain, possibly from ''fawney'' (a type of ring used in confidence tricks)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"phon (fake, from slang)","suffix":"-y (characterized by)"},"relatedWords":["phoniness","fake","fraud"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":47,"contextSentence":"I''m a total and utter phony."},{"word":"utter","phonetic":"/ˈʌt.ər/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"complete; absolute; total","meaningKo":"완전한, 순전한","etymology":"From Old English ''utera'' (outer, further)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"ut (out)","suffix":"-er (comparative)"},"relatedWords":["utterly","utterance"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":47,"contextSentence":"I''m a total and utter phony."},{"word":"vaguely","phonetic":"/ˈveɪɡ.li/","partOfSpeech":"adverb","definition":"in a way that is not clear or certain; somewhat","meaningKo":"막연하게, 어렴풋이","etymology":"From Latin ''vagus'' (wandering, uncertain)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"vagu (wandering)","suffix":"-ly (in the manner of)"},"relatedWords":["vague","vagueness"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":49,"contextSentence":"These are just words paired with vaguely thought-provoking stock photos."},{"word":"thought-provoking","phonetic":"/ˈθɔːt prəˌvoʊ.kɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"stimulating careful consideration or attention","meaningKo":"생각을 자극하는, 시사적인","etymology":"Compound of ''thought'' (Old English) + ''provoking'' (from Latin ''provocare'', to call forth)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"pro- (forth)","root":"voc (call)","suffix":"-ing (causing)"},"relatedWords":["provoke","provocative","thoughtful"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":49,"contextSentence":"These are just words paired with vaguely thought-provoking stock photos."},{"word":"gibberish","phonetic":"/ˈdʒɪb.ər.ɪʃ/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"unintelligible or meaningless speech or writing; nonsense","meaningKo":"횡설수설, 알아들을 수 없는 말","etymology":"Possibly from ''jabber'' or from Jabir ibn Hayyan (alchemist whose writings were obscure)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"gibber (speak rapidly)","suffix":"-ish (resembling)"},"relatedWords":["gibber","jabber","babble"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":51,"contextSentence":"I''m just going to start saying gibberish."},{"word":"satisfying","phonetic":"/ˈsæt.ɪs.faɪ.ɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"giving fulfillment or pleasure; meeting expectations","meaningKo":"만족스러운","etymology":"From Latin ''satisfacere'' (to do enough)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"satis (enough)","suffix":"-fying (making)"},"relatedWords":["satisfy","satisfaction","satisfactory"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":57,"contextSentence":"Like maybe, just maybe, I''m building to some sort of satisfying conclusion."},{"word":"gesticulating","phonetic":"/dʒɛˈstɪk.jə.leɪ.tɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"using gestures, especially dramatic ones, instead of or to emphasize speaking","meaningKo":"몸짓을 하는, 손짓으로 표현하는","etymology":"From Latin ''gesticulari'' (to gesture), from ''gesticulus'' (a mimic gesture)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"gest (carry, gesture)","suffix":"-iculating (repeatedly doing)"},"relatedWords":["gesture","gesticulation"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":58,"contextSentence":"I''m gesticulating as though I am."},{"word":"intensity","phonetic":"/ɪnˈten.sə.ti/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"the quality of being intense; great energy, strength, or concentration","meaningKo":"강도, 강렬함","etymology":"From Latin ''intensitas'', from ''intensus'' (stretched, strained)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"in- (into)","root":"tens (stretch)","suffix":"-ity (state of)"},"relatedWords":["intense","intensify","intensive"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":58,"contextSentence":"I''m pacing, I''m growing in intensity."},{"word":"gesture","phonetic":"/ˈdʒes.tʃər/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"a movement of part of the body to express an idea or meaning","meaningKo":"제스처, 손짓, 몸짓","etymology":"From Medieval Latin ''gestura'' (mode of action), from ''gerere'' (to carry, perform)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"gest (carry, perform)","suffix":"-ure (action or process)"},"relatedWords":["gesticulate","gesticulation"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":11,"contextSentence":"I''m going to make a lot of hand gestures."},{"word":"exceeds","phonetic":"/ɪkˈsiːdz/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"to be greater than; to surpass","meaningKo":"초과하다, 넘다","etymology":"From Latin ''excedere'' (to go beyond)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"ex- (out, beyond)","root":"ced (go)","suffix":"-s (third person)"},"relatedWords":["exceed","excess","excessive","exceedingly"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":40,"contextSentence":"The majority far exceeds the minority."},{"word":"panicking","phonetic":"/ˈpæn.ɪ.kɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"feeling sudden uncontrollable fear or anxiety","meaningKo":"당황하는, 공황에 빠진","etymology":"From Greek ''panikos'' (of or for Pan, the god who caused terror)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"pan (Pan, Greek god)","suffix":"-icking (present participle)"},"relatedWords":["panic","panicky"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":46,"contextSentence":"I''m floundering, panicking, I''ve got nothing."}]'::jsonb, '[{"pattern":"Be going to (Future Plans)","explanation":"''Be going to + verb'' is used to express future plans, intentions, or predictions. It implies a pre-decided plan.","explanationKo":"''be going to + 동사''는 미래의 계획, 의도 또는 예측을 표현할 때 사용합니다. 미리 정해진 계획을 암시합니다.","examples":["I''m going to get started with the opening.","I''m going to make a lot of hand gestures.","I''m going to do this with my right hand."],"segmentIndex":11},{"pattern":"Present Continuous for Ongoing Actions","explanation":"The present continuous (am/is/are + -ing) describes actions happening right now, giving a sense of immediacy and live narration.","explanationKo":"현재 진행형(am/is/are + -ing)은 지금 일어나고 있는 행동을 묘사하며, 즉시성과 실시간 서술의 느낌을 줍니다.","examples":["I''m floundering, panicking, I''ve got nothing.","I''m seeing some hands.","I''m pacing, I''m growing in intensity."],"segmentIndex":46},{"pattern":"Make it seem like (Creating False Impressions)","explanation":"''Make it seem like'' is used to describe creating a false appearance or impression. ''Make'' is a causative verb here.","explanationKo":"''Make it seem like''는 거짓 외양이나 인상을 만드는 것을 묘사합니다. 여기서 ''make''는 사역동사로 사용됩니다.","examples":["I will make it seem like I do.","I''d like it to seem like I''m making points.","I''m going to make it seem like I''m building to a moment."],"segmentIndex":9},{"pattern":"By show of hands (Polling Expressions)","explanation":"''By show of hands'' is a set phrase used to ask an audience to raise their hands to indicate agreement or experience.","explanationKo":"''By show of hands''는 청중에게 동의나 경험을 나타내기 위해 손을 들어달라고 요청할 때 쓰는 고정 표현입니다.","examples":["By show of hands, how many of you all have been asked a question before?"],"segmentIndex":14},{"pattern":"And yet (Contrasting Connector)","explanation":"''And yet'' introduces a surprising contrast or contradiction to what was previously stated. It is stronger than ''but''.","explanationKo":"''And yet''은 이전에 언급한 것과 놀라운 대조나 모순을 도입합니다. ''but''보다 강한 표현입니다.","examples":["And yet, through my manner of speaking, I will make it seem like I do."],"segmentIndex":8},{"pattern":"If you were... you might (Hypothetical Conditional)","explanation":"This second conditional structure (if + past tense, would/might + verb) describes an imaginary or unlikely situation and its probable result.","explanationKo":"이 2차 조건문 구조(if + 과거 시제, would/might + 동사)는 상상 속의 또는 가능성 낮은 상황과 그 예상 결과를 묘사합니다.","examples":["If you were, say, watching this on YouTube with the sound off, you might think, huh, okay."],"segmentIndex":44},{"pattern":"As though / As if (Manner Comparison)","explanation":"''As though'' and ''as if'' introduce clauses that describe how something appears, often implying it is not actually true.","explanationKo":"''as though''와 ''as if''는 무언가가 어떻게 보이는지를 묘사하는 절을 도입하며, 종종 실제로는 그렇지 않음을 암시합니다.","examples":["I''m gesticulating as though I am.","I''m going to point at them like I''m making use of my time."],"segmentIndex":58},{"pattern":"Maybe, just maybe (Emphatic Repetition)","explanation":"Repeating ''maybe'' with ''just'' inserted creates emphasis and dramatic effect, suggesting a hopeful but uncertain possibility.","explanationKo":"''maybe''를 반복하고 사이에 ''just''를 넣으면 강조와 극적인 효과를 만들어내며, 희망적이지만 불확실한 가능성을 제시합니다.","examples":["And maybe, just maybe, you will feel like you''ve learned something.","Like maybe, just maybe, I''m building to some sort of satisfying conclusion."],"segmentIndex":10},{"pattern":"I''d like you to (Polite Request)","explanation":"''I''d like you to + verb'' is a polite way to make a request or express a wish about what someone else should do.","explanationKo":"''I''d like you to + 동사''는 다른 사람이 해야 할 일에 대해 요청하거나 바람을 표현하는 정중한 방법입니다.","examples":["I''d like you to think about what you heard at the beginning.","I''d like it to seem like I''m making points."],"segmentIndex":64},{"pattern":"For one (Personal Opinion Marker)","explanation":"''For one'' is used after ''I'' to emphasize that you are stating your own personal opinion, often implying others may disagree.","explanationKo":"''for one''은 ''I'' 뒤에 사용되어 자신의 개인적인 의견을 강조하며, 종종 다른 사람들은 동의하지 않을 수 있음을 암시합니다.","examples":["But I, for one, have no idea who he is."],"segmentIndex":23},{"pattern":"What if (Speculative Question)","explanation":"''What if'' introduces a hypothetical question, asking the listener to imagine a possible scenario.","explanationKo":"''What if''는 가정적인 질문을 도입하여 청자에게 가능한 시나리오를 상상하도록 합니다.","examples":["And what if I was? Amazing, isn''t it?"],"segmentIndex":62},{"pattern":"If there''s one thing (Emphasis Phrase)","explanation":"''If there''s one thing you take away'' is a rhetorical structure used to highlight the single most important point in a speech.","explanationKo":"''If there''s one thing you take away''는 연설에서 가장 중요한 하나의 요점을 강조하기 위해 사용하는 수사적 구조입니다.","examples":["If there''s one thing you take away from my talk, I''d like you to think about what you heard at the beginning."],"segmentIndex":64}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"reduction","originalText":"I''m going to","phonetic":"/aɪm ˈɡʌnə/","koreanPhonetic":"아임 거나","explanation":"''Going to'' is reduced to ''gonna'' in fast speech. This is one of the most common reductions in spoken English.","explanationKo":"''going to''는 빠른 말에서 ''gonna''로 축약됩니다. 이것은 영어 구어에서 가장 흔한 축약 중 하나입니다.","practiceGuide":"''고잉 투'' 대신 ''거나''로 빠르게 발음하세요. ''I''m gonna''를 한 덩어리로 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":11},{"type":"linking","originalText":"kind of","phonetic":"/ˈkaɪn.dəv/","koreanPhonetic":"카인더브","explanation":"''Kind of'' links together where the ''d'' connects to ''of'', and ''of'' is reduced to /əv/. Often further reduced to ''kinda''.","explanationKo":"''kind of''에서 ''d''가 ''of''와 연결되고, ''of''는 /əv/로 약화됩니다. 종종 ''kinda''로 더 축약됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''카인드 오브'' 대신 ''카인더브'' 또는 ''카인다''로 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":18},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"a lot of","phonetic":"/ə ˈlɒ.ɾəv/","koreanPhonetic":"어 라러브","explanation":"The ''t'' in ''lot'' becomes a flap /ɾ/ before the vowel in ''of'', and ''of'' is reduced to /əv/.","explanationKo":"''lot''의 ''t''가 ''of''의 모음 앞에서 플랩 /ɾ/으로 변하고, ''of''는 /əv/로 약화됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''어 랏 오브'' 대신 ''어 라러브''로 자연스럽게 연결하세요.","segmentIndex":11},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"you''ve","phonetic":"/juːv/","koreanPhonetic":"유브","explanation":"''You have'' contracts to ''you''ve'', reducing ''have'' to just the /v/ sound attached to ''you''.","explanationKo":"''you have''가 ''you''ve''로 축약되어, ''have''가 ''you''에 붙는 /v/ 소리로만 남습니다.","practiceGuide":"''유 해브'' 대신 ''유브''로 한 음절로 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":10},{"type":"linking","originalText":"what I am","phonetic":"/wɒ.ɾaɪ.æm/","koreanPhonetic":"와라이앰","explanation":"The ''t'' in ''what'' becomes a flap /ɾ/ before the vowel in ''I'', and all three words flow together smoothly.","explanationKo":"''what''의 ''t''가 ''I''의 모음 앞에서 플랩 /ɾ/으로 변하고, 세 단어가 매끄럽게 이어집니다.","practiceGuide":"''왓 아이 앰'' 대신 ''와라이앰''으로 끊김 없이 연결하세요.","segmentIndex":9},{"type":"elision","originalText":"that''s nothing","phonetic":"/ðæts ˈnʌθ.ɪŋ/","koreanPhonetic":"댓츠 나띵","explanation":"The ''ts'' cluster at the end of ''that''s'' runs directly into ''nothing''. The vowel in ''nothing'' is reduced.","explanationKo":"''that''s'' 끝의 ''ts'' 자음군이 ''nothing''으로 바로 이어집니다. ''nothing''의 모음이 약화됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''댓츠''와 ''나띵''을 빠르게 연결하여 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":1},{"type":"assimilation","originalText":"hand gestures","phonetic":"/hæŋ ˈdʒes.tʃərz/","koreanPhonetic":"행 제스처즈","explanation":"The ''nd'' at the end of ''hand'' assimilates where the ''n'' becomes /ŋ/ before the velar-like beginning of ''gestures'', and the ''d'' is partially dropped.","explanationKo":"''hand'' 끝의 ''nd''에서 ''n''이 ''gestures''의 시작 앞에서 /ŋ/으로 동화되고, ''d''는 부분적으로 탈락합니다.","practiceGuide":"''핸드 제스처즈'' 대신 ''행 제스처즈''로 ''d''를 거의 생략하고 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":11},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"want to","phonetic":"/ˈwɒn.ə/","koreanPhonetic":"워나","explanation":"''Want to'' is commonly reduced to ''wanna'' in casual speech, dropping the ''t'' sound entirely.","explanationKo":"''want to''는 일상 대화에서 ''t'' 소리를 완전히 생략하고 ''wanna''로 축약됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''원트 투'' 대신 ''워나''로 발음하세요. ''t'' 소리를 생략하는 것이 핵심입니다.","segmentIndex":44},{"type":"linking","originalText":"take away","phonetic":"/ˈteɪ.kə.weɪ/","koreanPhonetic":"테이커웨이","explanation":"The ''k'' at the end of ''take'' links directly to the vowel at the start of ''away'', creating a smooth connection.","explanationKo":"''take'' 끝의 ''k''가 ''away'' 시작의 모음과 직접 연결되어 매끄러운 연결이 만들어집니다.","practiceGuide":"''테이크 어웨이'' 대신 ''테이커웨이''로 끊김 없이 연결하세요.","segmentIndex":64},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"I''ve got","phonetic":"/aɪv ˈɡɒt/","koreanPhonetic":"아이브 갓","explanation":"''I have got'' reduces to ''I''ve got'' where ''have'' becomes just /v/ sound. This is an informal way to say ''I have''.","explanationKo":"''I have got''이 ''I''ve got''으로 축약되어 ''have''가 /v/ 소리만 남습니다. ''I have''의 비격식 표현입니다.","practiceGuide":"''아이 해브 갓'' 대신 ''아이브 갓''으로 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":46},{"type":"linking","originalText":"reel you","phonetic":"/ˈriːl.juː/","koreanPhonetic":"릴유","explanation":"The ''l'' at the end of ''reel'' links directly to the ''y'' sound of ''you'', creating a fluid transition.","explanationKo":"''reel'' 끝의 ''l''이 ''you''의 ''y'' 소리와 직접 연결되어 유창한 전환을 만듭니다.","practiceGuide":"''릴''과 ''유''를 끊지 말고 ''릴유''로 이어서 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":21},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"let''s take a look at","phonetic":"/lɛts ˈteɪ.kə ˈlʊ.kət/","koreanPhonetic":"렛츠 테이커 루컫","explanation":"This common phrase runs together: ''take a'' links as /teɪkə/ and ''look at'' reduces with the final ''t'' weakening.","explanationKo":"이 흔한 구문이 이어져 발음됩니다: ''take a''가 /teɪkə/로 연결되고 ''look at''은 마지막 ''t''가 약화됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''렛츠 테이크 어 룩 앳'' 대신 ''렛츠 테이커 루컫''으로 한 호흡에 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":27},{"type":"assimilation","originalText":"in reality","phonetic":"/ɪn ri.ˈæl.ə.ti/","koreanPhonetic":"인 리앨러티","explanation":"The ''n'' at the end of ''in'' connects smoothly to the ''r'' of ''reality''. The phrase flows as one unit.","explanationKo":"''in'' 끝의 ''n''이 ''reality''의 ''r''과 부드럽게 연결됩니다. 구문이 하나의 단위로 흐릅니다.","practiceGuide":"''인''과 ''리앨러티''를 끊지 말고 하나의 덩어리로 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":26},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"by the way","phonetic":"/baɪ.ðə.ˈweɪ/","koreanPhonetic":"바이더웨이","explanation":"''By the way'' is spoken as a single unit where ''the'' is reduced to /ðə/ and all words blend together.","explanationKo":"''by the way''는 하나의 단위로 발음되며 ''the''가 /ðə/로 약화되고 모든 단어가 섞입니다.","practiceGuide":"세 단어를 따로 발음하지 말고 ''바이더웨이''로 한 덩어리로 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":58},{"type":"linking","originalText":"think about","phonetic":"/ˈθɪŋ.kə.baʊt/","koreanPhonetic":"띵커바웃","explanation":"The ''k'' sound at the end of ''think'' links to the vowel ''a'' in ''about'', and ''about'' reduces its first syllable.","explanationKo":"''think'' 끝의 ''k'' 소리가 ''about''의 모음 ''a''와 연결되고, ''about''의 첫 음절이 약화됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''띵크 어바웃'' 대신 ''띵커바웃''으로 매끄럽게 연결하세요.","segmentIndex":64}]'::jsonb, '{"sections":[{"section":"Introduction / Hook","startSegment":0,"endSegment":10,"summary":"Will Stephen opens by declaring he has absolutely nothing to say, but promises that his manner of speaking will make it seem brilliant.","summaryKo":"윌 스티븐은 할 말이 전혀 없다고 선언하면서 시작하지만, 말하는 방식을 통해 훌륭하게 들리게 만들겠다고 약속합니다.","keyPoints":["연사가 아무 내용 없이 시작한다는 역설적 도입","말하는 방식만으로 똑똑하게 들릴 수 있다는 주제 제시","청중에게 무언가를 배운 것 같은 느낌이 들 것이라는 예고"]},{"section":"Opening Technique Demonstration","startSegment":11,"endSegment":20,"summary":"He demonstrates common TEDx opening techniques: hand gestures, audience polling, personal anecdotes, and emotional connection—while openly narrating what he''s doing.","summaryKo":"손동작, 청중 설문, 개인적 일화, 감정적 연결 등 일반적인 TEDx 오프닝 기법을 시연하면서, 자신이 하고 있는 것을 공개적으로 설명합니다.","keyPoints":["손동작과 안경 만지기 같은 비언어적 기법 소개","거수 투표를 통한 청중 참여 유도","개인적 일화로 긴장을 풀고 호감을 얻는 전략 설명"]},{"section":"Building Authority with Visuals","startSegment":21,"endSegment":42,"summary":"He shows how speakers use images, numbers, and graphs to appear credible—displaying random numbers, meaningless pie charts, and bar graphs to satirize data-driven presentations.","summaryKo":"이미지, 숫자, 그래프를 사용하여 신뢰감을 주는 방법을 보여줍니다—무작위 숫자, 의미 없는 원형 차트와 막대 그래프를 통해 데이터 기반 프레젠테이션을 풍자합니다.","keyPoints":["구글 이미지 검색한 ''과학자'' 사진으로 지적인 느낌 연출","의미 없는 숫자들로 데이터 제시 방식 패러디","원형 차트와 막대 그래프로 시각 자료의 설득력 풍자"]},{"section":"Confession and Commitment","startSegment":43,"endSegment":48,"summary":"He confesses he''s a complete phony who is panicking and floundering, but declares he was offered a TED talk and will see it through.","summaryKo":"자신이 당황하고 허둥대는 완전한 사기꾼이라고 고백하지만, TED 강연 제안을 받았으니 끝까지 하겠다고 선언합니다.","keyPoints":["사기꾼이라는 솔직한 고백으로 역설적 진정성 확보","유튜브 무음 시청 시 전문가처럼 보일 것이라는 관찰","끝까지 해내겠다는 유머러스한 결의"]},{"section":"Descent into Nonsense","startSegment":49,"endSegment":59,"summary":"He shows stock photos with meaningless words, then descends into complete gibberish, while maintaining the physical mannerisms of a compelling speaker.","summaryKo":"의미 없는 단어와 사진을 보여주다가 완전한 횡설수설로 내려가면서도, 매력적인 연사의 물리적 매너리즘은 유지합니다.","keyPoints":["사진과 단어의 무의미한 조합으로 시각 자료 풍자","횡설수설하면서도 제스처와 페이싱으로 의미 있어 보이게 하기","프레임 안경을 쓴 것을 공개하며 외모 조작 폭로"]},{"section":"Climax and Conclusion","startSegment":60,"endSegment":70,"summary":"He slows down and builds to a mock-emotional conclusion, pointing out that both the beginning and end of his talk contain nothing—and that''s the entire point.","summaryKo":"속도를 늦추고 가짜 감동적 결론을 향해 나아가며, 강연의 처음과 끝 모두 아무것도 없다는 것이 바로 요점이라고 지적합니다.","keyPoints":["톤 변화와 속도 조절로 감동적인 순간 연출","처음과 끝 모두 아무것도 없었다는 메타적 결론","청중에게 생각하라거나 안 해도 된다는 유머러스한 마무리"]}],"signalExpressions":[{"expression":"Hear that?","type":"hook","segmentIndex":1,"role":"청중의 주의를 환기하는 오프닝 질문으로, 호기심을 유발합니다."},{"expression":"And yet","type":"transition","segmentIndex":8,"role":"앞의 내용(아무것도 없음)에서 반전(그럼에도 똑똑하게 들리게 하겠다)으로 전환합니다."},{"expression":"Now, I''m going to get started with","type":"transition","segmentIndex":11,"role":"도입부에서 본격적인 시연으로 넘어가는 전환 표현입니다."},{"expression":"By show of hands","type":"hook","segmentIndex":14,"role":"청중 참여를 유도하는 고전적인 프레젠테이션 기법입니다."},{"expression":"And now, I''m going to bring it to a broader point","type":"transition","segmentIndex":20,"role":"개인적인 이야기에서 더 넓은 주제로 전환하는 신호 표현입니다."},{"expression":"Now, if you don''t believe me, let''s take a look at the numbers","type":"transition","segmentIndex":27,"role":"주장에서 증거 제시로 전환하며 신뢰성을 구축하는 표현입니다."},{"expression":"And to follow that up","type":"transition","segmentIndex":39,"role":"숫자 데이터에서 그래프 시각 자료로 넘어가는 연결 표현입니다."},{"expression":"But you know what?","type":"transition","segmentIndex":47,"role":"고백에서 결의로 전환하는 구어적 전환 표현입니다."},{"expression":"And now I''m going to slow things down a little bit","type":"transition","segmentIndex":60,"role":"페이스를 바꾸며 결론부로 진입하는 전환 신호입니다."},{"expression":"If there''s one thing you take away from my talk","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":64,"role":"핵심 메시지를 요약하며 결론으로 향하는 고전적인 마무리 표현입니다."},{"expression":"Think about that. Or don''t, that''s fine.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":67,"role":"유머러스한 반전으로 전통적인 TED 마무리를 패러디합니다."},{"expression":"And now I''m going to stop talking.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":68,"role":"강연의 끝을 직접적으로 알리는 솔직한 마무리 표현입니다."}]}'::jsonb
)
