n":"Make the big choices in life. Because almost everything, all external expectations, all pride,","textKo":"제가 만난 가장 중요한 도구입니다. 왜냐하면 거의 모든 것, 모든 외부의 기대, 모든 자존심,","words":[{"word":"make","start":520.96,"end":521.2},{"word":"the","start":521.2,"end":521.34},{"word":"big","start":521.34,"end":521.48},{"word":"choices","start":521.48,"end":521.88},{"word":"in","start":521.88,"end":522.12},{"word":"life.","start":522.12,"end":522.44},{"word":"Because","start":523.14,"end":523.68},{"word":"almost","start":523.68,"end":524.02},{"word":"everything,","start":524.02,"end":524.58},{"word":"all","start":524.86,"end":525.54},{"word":"external","start":525.54,"end":526.0},{"word":"expectations,","start":526.0,"end":526.74},{"word":"all","start":527.16,"end":527.34},{"word":"pride,","start":527.34,"end":527.74}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":84,"start":528.24,"end":532.96,"textEn":"All fear of embarrassment or failure, these things just fall away in the face of death,","textKo":"창피하거나 실패에 대한 모든 두려움, 이런 것들은 죽음 앞에서 그냥 사라지기 때문입니다.","words":[{"word":"all","start":528.24,"end":528.44},{"word":"fear","start":528.44,"end":528.68},{"word":"of","start":528.68,"end":528.82},{"word":"embarrassment","start":528.82,"end":529.26},{"word":"or","start":529.26,"end":529.46},{"word":"failure,","start":529.46,"end":529.84},{"word":"these","start":530.12,"end":530.58},{"word":"things","start":530.58,"end":530.84},{"word":"just","start":530.84,"end":531.06},{"word":"fall","start":531.06,"end":531.44},{"word":"away","start":531.44,"end":531.8},{"word":"in","start":531.8,"end":532.14},{"word":"the","start":532.14,"end":532.24},{"word":"face","start":532.24,"end":532.44},{"word":"of","start":532.44,"end":532.62},{"word":"death,","start":532.62,"end":532.96}],"listenDifficulty":3},{"index":85,"start":532.96,"end":539.76,"textEn":"Leaving only what is truly important. Remembering that you are going to die is the best way I know","textKo":"진정으로 중요한 것만 남깁니다. 죽을 것이라는 것을 기억하는 것은 잃을 것이 있다고","words":[{"word":"leaving","start":532.96,"end":533.9},{"word":"only","start":533.9,"end":534.3},{"word":"what","start":534.3,"end":534.48},{"word":"is","start":534.48,"end":534.62},{"word":"truly","start":534.62,"end":534.92},{"word":"important.","start":534.92,"end":535.48},{"word":"Remembering","start":536.32,"end":536.9},{"word":"that","start":536.9,"end":537.06},{"word":"you","start":537.06,"end":537.2},{"word":"are","start":537.2,"end":537.36},{"word":"going","start":537.36,"end":537.56},{"word":"to","start":537.56,"end":537.74},{"word":"die","start":537.74,"end":538.12},{"word":"is","start":538.12,"end":538.74},{"word":"the","start":538.74,"end":538.86},{"word":"best","start":538.86,"end":539.08},{"word":"way","start":539.08,"end":539.28},{"word":"I","start":539.28,"end":539.44},{"word":"know","start":539.44,"end":539.76}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":86,"start":539.76,"end":546.36,"textEn":"To avoid the trap of thinking you have something to lose. You are already naked. There is no reason","textKo":"생각하는 함정을 피하는 제가 아는 최고의 방법입니다. 여러분은 이미 벌거벗은 것입니다. 마음을 따르지 않을 이유가 없습니다.","words":[{"word":"to","start":539.76,"end":540.12},{"word":"avoid","start":540.12,"end":540.46},{"word":"the","start":540.46,"end":540.64},{"word":"trap","start":540.64,"end":540.9},{"word":"of","start":540.9,"end":541.14},{"word":"thinking","start":541.14,"end":541.44},{"word":"you","start":541.44,"end":541.86},{"word":"have","start":541.86,"end":541.98},{"word":"something","start":541.98,"end":542.34},{"word":"to","start":542.34,"end":542.56},{"word":"lose.","start":542.56,"end":542.92},{"word":"You","start":543.4,"end":543.84},{"word":"are","start":543.84,"end":544.0},{"word":"already","start":544.0,"end":544.46},{"word":"naked.","start":544.46,"end":544.88},{"word":"There","start":545.22,"end":545.66},{"word":"is","start":545.66,"end":545.8},{"word":"no","start":545.8,"end":545.98},{"word":"reason","start":545.98,"end":546.36}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":87,"start":546.36,"end":555.04,"textEn":"Not to follow your heart. No one wants to die. Even people who want to go to heaven don''t want to die to","textKo":"아무도 죽고 싶어하지 않습니다. 천국에 가고 싶은 사람들조차 죽어서 가고 싶지는 않습니다.","words":[{"word":"not","start":546.36,"end":546.84},{"word":"to","start":546.84,"end":547.0},{"word":"follow","start":547.0,"end":547.3},{"word":"your","start":547.3,"end":547.52},{"word":"heart.","start":547.52,"end":547.8},{"word":"No","start":549.54,"end":550.12},{"word":"one","start":550.12,"end":550.44},{"word":"wants","start":550.44,"end":551.04},{"word":"to","start":551.04,"end":551.2},{"word":"die.","start":551.2,"end":551.52},{"word":"Even","start":552.0,"end":552.58},{"word":"people","start":552.58,"end":552.94},{"word":"who","start":552.94,"end":553.08},{"word":"want","start":553.08,"end":553.26},{"word":"to","start":553.26,"end":553.38},{"word":"go","start":553.38,"end":553.48},{"word":"to","start":553.48,"end":553.62},{"word":"heaven","start":553.62,"end":553.9},{"word":"don''t","start":553.9,"end":554.48},{"word":"want","start":554.48,"end":554.58},{"word":"to","start":554.58,"end":554.7},{"word":"die","start":554.7,"end":554.9},{"word":"to","start":554.9,"end":555.04}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":88,"start":555.04,"end":563.56,"textEn":"Get there. And yet, death is the destination we all share. No one has ever escaped it. And that is as it","textKo":"그런데도 죽음은 우리 모두가 공유하는 목적지입니다. 아무도 그것을 피한 적이 없습니다. 그리고 그것이","words":[{"word":"get","start":555.04,"end":555.2},{"word":"there.","start":555.2,"end":555.44},{"word":"And","start":556.12,"end":556.64},{"word":"yet,","start":556.64,"end":556.88},{"word":"death","start":557.14,"end":557.9},{"word":"is","start":557.9,"end":558.08},{"word":"the","start":558.08,"end":558.22},{"word":"destination","start":558.22,"end":558.66},{"word":"we","start":558.66,"end":559.02},{"word":"all","start":559.02,"end":559.22},{"word":"share.","start":559.22,"end":559.62},{"word":"No","start":560.02,"end":560.54},{"word":"one","start":560.54,"end":560.66},{"word":"has","start":560.66,"end":560.82},{"word":"ever","start":560.82,"end":561.06},{"word":"escaped","start":561.06,"end":561.48},{"word":"it.","start":561.48,"end":561.74},{"word":"And","start":562.04,"end":562.56},{"word":"that","start":562.56,"end":562.72},{"word":"is","start":562.72,"end":562.98},{"word":"as","start":562.98,"end":563.42},{"word":"it","start":563.42,"end":563.56}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":89,"start":563.56,"end":570.96,"textEn":"Should be. Because death is very likely the single best invention of life. It''s life''s change agent. It","textKo":"마땅합니다. 왜냐하면 죽음은 아마도 생명의 가장 훌륭한 발명이기 때문입니다. 생명의 변화의 동력입니다. 그것은","words":[{"word":"should","start":563.56,"end":563.8},{"word":"be.","start":563.8,"end":564.1},{"word":"Because","start":564.34,"end":564.8},{"word":"death","start":564.8,"end":565.14},{"word":"is","start":565.14,"end":565.64},{"word":"very","start":565.64,"end":565.9},{"word":"likely","start":565.9,"end":566.3},{"word":"the","start":566.3,"end":566.5},{"word":"single","start":566.5,"end":566.84},{"word":"best","start":566.84,"end":567.14},{"word":"invention","start":567.14,"end":567.7},{"word":"of","start":567.7,"end":568.04},{"word":"life.","start":568.04,"end":568.34},{"word":"It''s","start":568.94,"end":569.46},{"word":"life''s","start":569.46,"end":569.8},{"word":"change","start":569.8,"end":570.2},{"word":"agent.","start":570.2,"end":570.6},{"word":"It","start":570.76,"end":570.96}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":90,"start":570.96,"end":578.5,"textEn":"Clears out the old to make way for the new. Right now, the new is you. But someday, not too long from now,","textKo":"낡은 것을 치우고 새것을 위한 자리를 만듭니다. 지금 새것은 여러분입니다. 하지만 언젠가, 그리 멀지 않은 미래에,","words":[{"word":"clears","start":570.96,"end":571.28},{"word":"out","start":571.28,"end":571.46},{"word":"the","start":571.46,"end":571.62},{"word":"old","start":571.62,"end":571.84},{"word":"to","start":571.84,"end":572.04},{"word":"make","start":572.04,"end":572.18},{"word":"way","start":572.18,"end":572.38},{"word":"for","start":572.38,"end":572.54},{"word":"the","start":572.54,"end":572.64},{"word":"new.","start":572.64,"end":572.86},{"word":"Right","start":573.72,"end":574.24},{"word":"now,","start":574.24,"end":574.5},{"word":"the","start":574.76,"end":574.94},{"word":"new","start":574.94,"end":575.14},{"word":"is","start":575.14,"end":575.42},{"word":"you.","start":575.42,"end":575.7},{"word":"But","start":576.4,"end":576.92},{"word":"someday,","start":576.92,"end":577.36},{"word":"not","start":577.5,"end":577.6},{"word":"too","start":577.6,"end":577.78},{"word":"long","start":577.78,"end":578.02},{"word":"from","start":578.02,"end":578.22},{"word":"now,","start":578.22,"end":578.5}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":91,"start":578.5,"end":585.2,"textEn":"You will gradually become the old and be cleared away. Sorry to be so dramatic, but it''s quite true.","textKo":"여러분도 점차 낡은 것이 되어 치워질 것입니다. 너무 극적이어서 죄송하지만, 사실입니다.","words":[{"word":"you","start":578.5,"end":578.86},{"word":"will","start":578.86,"end":579.02},{"word":"gradually","start":579.02,"end":579.42},{"word":"become","start":579.42,"end":579.78},{"word":"the","start":579.78,"end":579.94},{"word":"old","start":579.94,"end":580.24},{"word":"and","start":580.24,"end":580.74},{"word":"be","start":580.74,"end":580.9},{"word":"cleared","start":580.9,"end":581.16},{"word":"away.","start":581.16,"end":581.46},{"word":"Sorry","start":582.3,"end":582.9},{"word":"to","start":582.9,"end":583.02},{"word":"be","start":583.02,"end":583.12},{"word":"so","start":583.12,"end":583.32},{"word":"dramatic,","start":583.32,"end":583.74},{"word":"but","start":584.04,"end":584.56},{"word":"it''s","start":584.56,"end":584.7},{"word":"quite","start":584.7,"end":584.9},{"word":"true.","start":584.9,"end":585.2}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":92,"start":586.38,"end":593.64,"textEn":"Your time is limited, so don''t waste it living someone else''s life. Don''t be trapped by dogma,","textKo":"여러분의 시간은 한정되어 있으니, 다른 사람의 인생을 사는 데 낭비하지 마세요. 독단에 갇히지 마세요.","words":[{"word":"Your","start":586.38,"end":586.98},{"word":"time","start":586.98,"end":587.28},{"word":"is","start":587.28,"end":587.52},{"word":"limited,","start":587.52,"end":587.84},{"word":"so","start":588.18,"end":588.5},{"word":"don''t","start":588.5,"end":588.94},{"word":"waste","start":588.94,"end":589.26},{"word":"it","start":589.26,"end":589.52},{"word":"living","start":589.52,"end":589.78},{"word":"someone","start":589.78,"end":590.28},{"word":"else''s","start":590.28,"end":590.82},{"word":"life.","start":590.82,"end":591.16},{"word":"Don''t","start":591.8,"end":592.4},{"word":"be","start":592.4,"end":592.52},{"word":"trapped","start":592.52,"end":592.84},{"word":"by","start":592.84,"end":593.08},{"word":"dogma,","start":593.08,"end":593.64}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":93,"start":593.74,"end":599.14,"textEn":"Which is living with the results of other people''s thinking. Don''t let the noise of others'' opinions","textKo":"그것은 다른 사람들의 생각의 결과로 사는 것입니다. 다른 사람들의 의견이라는 소음이","words":[{"word":"which","start":593.74,"end":594.1},{"word":"is","start":594.1,"end":594.24},{"word":"living","start":594.24,"end":594.48},{"word":"with","start":594.48,"end":594.66},{"word":"the","start":594.66,"end":594.76},{"word":"results","start":594.76,"end":595.1},{"word":"of","start":595.1,"end":595.3},{"word":"other","start":595.3,"end":595.56},{"word":"people''s","start":595.56,"end":596.02},{"word":"thinking.","start":596.02,"end":596.34},{"word":"Don''t","start":596.96,"end":597.56},{"word":"let","start":597.56,"end":597.68},{"word":"the","start":597.68,"end":597.84},{"word":"noise","start":597.84,"end":598.18},{"word":"of","start":598.18,"end":598.36},{"word":"others''","start":598.36,"end":598.6},{"word":"opinions","start":598.74,"end":599.14}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":94,"start":599.14,"end":605.0,"textEn":"Drown out your own inner voice. And most important, have the courage to follow your heart and intuition.","textKo":"여러분 자신의 내면의 목소리를 삼키지 못하게 하세요. 그리고 가장 중요한 것은, 마음과 직감을 따를 용기를 가지세요.","words":[{"word":"drown","start":599.14,"end":599.44},{"word":"out","start":599.44,"end":599.66},{"word":"your","start":599.66,"end":599.84},{"word":"own","start":599.84,"end":600.06},{"word":"inner","start":600.06,"end":600.3},{"word":"voice.","start":600.3,"end":600.7},{"word":"And","start":601.18,"end":601.6},{"word":"most","start":601.6,"end":601.86},{"word":"important,","start":601.86,"end":602.34},{"word":"have","start":602.66,"end":602.92},{"word":"the","start":602.92,"end":603.04},{"word":"courage","start":603.04,"end":603.32},{"word":"to","start":603.32,"end":603.54},{"word":"follow","start":603.54,"end":603.84},{"word":"your","start":603.84,"end":604.04},{"word":"heart","start":604.04,"end":604.32},{"word":"and","start":604.32,"end":604.52},{"word":"intuition.","start":604.52,"end":605.0}],"listenDifficulty":2},{"index":95,"start":605.0,"end":611.92,"textEn":"They somehow already know what you truly want to become. Everything else is secondary.","textKo":"그것들은 이미 여러분이 진정으로 무엇이 되고 싶은지 어떻게든 알고 있습니다. 다른 모든 것은 부차적입니다.","words":[{"word":"They","start":605.0,"end":605.84},{"word":"somehow","start":605.84,"end":606.26},{"word":"already","start":606.26,"end":606.76},{"word":"know","start":606.76,"end":607.14},{"word":"what","start":607.14,"end":607.76},{"word":"you","start":607.76,"end":607.9},{"word":"truly","start":607.9,"end":608.28},{"word":"want","start":608.28,"end":608.6},{"word":"to","start":608.6,"end":608.76},{"word":"become.","start":608.76,"end":609.1},{"word":"Everything","start":609.6,"end":610.32},{"word":"else","start":610.32,"end":610.7},{"word":"is","start":610.7,"end":611.38},{"word":"secondary.","start":611.38,"end":611.92}],"listenDifficulty":1},{"index":96,"start":613.96,"end":616.08,"textEn":"Stay hungry. Stay foolish.","textKo":"항상 갈망하세요. 우직하게 나아가세요.","words":[{"word":"Stay","start":613.8,"end":614.26},{"word":"hungry.","start":614.26,"end":614.66},{"word":"Stay","start":615.04,"end":615.7},{"word":"foolish.","start":615.7,"end":616.08}],"listenDifficulty":1}]}'::jsonb, '[{"word":"commencement","phonetic":"/kəˈmɛnsmənt/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A ceremony at which degrees or diplomas are conferred; a graduation ceremony","meaningKo":"졸업식, 학위 수여식","etymology":"From Old French ''commencement'', from ''comencier'' (to begin)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"com-","root":"menc (begin)","suffix":"-ment"},"relatedWords":["commence","commencement address","beginning"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":0,"contextSentence":"Steve Jobs delivered a commencement address at Stanford University."},{"word":"adoption","phonetic":"/əˈdɑːpʃən/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"The act of legally taking another''s child and raising it as one''s own","meaningKo":"입양","etymology":"From Latin ''adoptio'', from ''adoptare'' (to choose for oneself)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"ad-","root":"opt (choose)","suffix":"-ion"},"relatedWords":["adopt","adoptive","adoptee"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":4,"contextSentence":"She decided to put me up for adoption."},{"word":"unwed","phonetic":"/ˌʌnˈwɛd/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"Not married","meaningKo":"미혼의","etymology":"From Old English ''un-'' (not) + ''weddian'' (to pledge)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"un-","root":"wed (marry)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["unmarried","single","wedding"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":4,"contextSentence":"My biological mother was a young, unwed graduate student."},{"word":"relent","phonetic":"/rɪˈlɛnt/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"To become less severe or intense; to finally agree after initially refusing","meaningKo":"누그러지다, 마음을 바꾸다","etymology":"From Latin ''re-'' (back) + ''lentare'' (to bend)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"re-","root":"lent (bend, soften)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["relentless","unrelenting"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":11,"contextSentence":"She only relented a few months later when my parents promised that I would go to college."},{"word":"naively","phonetic":"/naɪˈiːvli/","partOfSpeech":"adverb","definition":"In a way that shows a lack of experience, wisdom, or judgment","meaningKo":"순진하게, 어리석게","etymology":"From French ''naïf'' (natural, innocent), from Latin ''nativus'' (native)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"naïve (innocent)","suffix":"-ly"},"relatedWords":["naive","naivety","ingenuousness"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":13,"contextSentence":"But I naively chose a college that was almost as expensive as Stanford."},{"word":"calligraphy","phonetic":"/kəˈlɪɡrəfi/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"The art of producing decorative handwriting or lettering with a pen or brush","meaningKo":"서예, 캘리그래피","etymology":"From Greek ''kallos'' (beauty) + ''graphein'' (to write)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"calli (beautiful) + graph (write)","suffix":"-y"},"relatedWords":["calligrapher","typography","penmanship"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":26,"contextSentence":"Reed College at that time offered perhaps the best calligraphy instruction in the country."},{"word":"serif","phonetic":"/ˈsɛrɪf/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A small line or stroke attached to the end of a larger stroke in a letter or symbol in certain typefaces","meaningKo":"세리프 (글자 획 끝의 장식선)","etymology":"Possibly from Dutch ''schreef'' (a line, stroke)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"serif (line)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["sans-serif","typeface","font"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":29,"contextSentence":"I learned about serif and sans-serif typefaces."},{"word":"typography","phonetic":"/taɪˈpɑːɡrəfi/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"The art and technique of arranging type to make written language legible, readable, and appealing","meaningKo":"타이포그래피, 활자 배열술","etymology":"From Greek ''typos'' (impression) + ''graphein'' (to write)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"typo (type, impression) + graph (write)","suffix":"-y"},"relatedWords":["typographer","typographic","typeface"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":31,"contextSentence":"It was beautiful, historical, artistically subtle in a way that science can''t capture."},{"word":"intuition","phonetic":"/ˌɪntjuˈɪʃən/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"The ability to understand something instinctively, without the need for conscious reasoning","meaningKo":"직감, 직관","etymology":"From Latin ''intueri'' (to look at, consider)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"in-","root":"tuit (look at)","suffix":"-ion"},"relatedWords":["intuitive","intuit","intuitively"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":25,"contextSentence":"Curiosity and intuition turned out to be priceless later on."},{"word":"diverge","phonetic":"/daɪˈvɜːrdʒ/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"To separate from another route or path; to differ or deviate in opinion or direction","meaningKo":"갈라지다, 벗어나다","etymology":"From Latin ''di-'' (apart) + ''vergere'' (to turn, bend)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"di-","root":"verge (turn)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["divergence","divergent","converge"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":51,"contextSentence":"But then our visions of the future began to diverge."},{"word":"devastating","phonetic":"/ˈdɛvəsteɪtɪŋ/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"Highly destructive or damaging; causing severe shock, distress, or grief","meaningKo":"충격적인, 엄청난 타격을 주는","etymology":"From Latin ''devastare'' (to lay waste)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"de-","root":"vast (lay waste)","suffix":"-ating"},"relatedWords":["devastate","devastation","devastating blow"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":53,"contextSentence":"What had been the focus of my entire adult life was gone. And it was devastating."},{"word":"entrepreneur","phonetic":"/ˌɑːntrəprəˈnɜːr/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A person who organizes and operates a business, taking on greater than normal financial risks","meaningKo":"기업가, 사업가","etymology":"From French ''entreprendre'' (to undertake)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"entre-","root":"prend (take)","suffix":"-eur"},"relatedWords":["entrepreneurial","entrepreneurship","enterprise"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":55,"contextSentence":"I felt that I had let the previous generation of entrepreneurs down."},{"word":"renaissance","phonetic":"/ˈrɛnəsɑːns/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A revival of or renewed interest in something; a period of new growth or activity","meaningKo":"르네상스, 부흥, 재탄생","etymology":"From French ''renaissance'' (rebirth), from Latin ''re-'' (again) + ''nasci'' (to be born)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"re-","root":"naiss (be born)","suffix":"-ance"},"relatedWords":["renew","rebirth","revival"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":67,"contextSentence":"The technology we developed at Next is at the heart of Apple''s current renaissance."},{"word":"dogma","phonetic":"/ˈdɒɡmə/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A principle or set of principles laid down by an authority as incontrovertibly true","meaningKo":"독단, 교리, 도그마","etymology":"From Greek ''dogma'' (opinion, belief), from ''dokein'' (to seem good)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"dogma (opinion, decree)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["dogmatic","dogmatism","doctrine"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":92,"contextSentence":"Don''t be trapped by dogma, which is living with the results of other people''s thinking."},{"word":"proportionally","phonetic":"/prəˈpɔːrʃənəli/","partOfSpeech":"adverb","definition":"In a way that corresponds in size or amount to something else; in proper proportion","meaningKo":"비례적으로","etymology":"From Latin ''proportio'' (comparative relation)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"pro-","root":"portion (part, share)","suffix":"-ally"},"relatedWords":["proportion","proportional","disproportionate"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":36,"contextSentence":"The Mac would have never had multiple typefaces or proportionally spaced fonts."},{"word":"baton","phonetic":"/bəˈtɒn/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A stick or staff passed from runner to runner in a relay race; figuratively, a responsibility passed on","meaningKo":"바통, (이어달리기의) 봉","etymology":"From French ''bâton'' (stick, staff)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"baton (stick)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["relay","pass the baton","conductor''s baton"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":55,"contextSentence":"That I had dropped the baton as it was being passed to me."},{"word":"stumble","phonetic":"/ˈstʌmbəl/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"To trip or momentarily lose one''s balance; to come across or find something by chance","meaningKo":"우연히 발견하다, 비틀거리다","etymology":"From Middle English ''stumblen'', related to Old Norse ''stumra''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"stumble (trip)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["stumble upon","stumbling block","stagger"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":24,"contextSentence":"Much of what I stumbled into by following my curiosity turned out to be priceless."},{"word":"priceless","phonetic":"/ˈpraɪsləs/","partOfSpeech":"adjective","definition":"So precious that its value cannot be determined; invaluable","meaningKo":"값을 매길 수 없는, 매우 귀중한","etymology":"From ''price'' + ''-less'' (without)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"price (value)","suffix":"-less"},"relatedWords":["invaluable","precious","worthless"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":25,"contextSentence":"Curiosity and intuition turned out to be priceless later on."},{"word":"karma","phonetic":"/ˈkɑːrmə/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"The sum of a person''s actions in this and previous states of existence, viewed as deciding their fate; destiny or fate","meaningKo":"카르마, 업보","etymology":"From Sanskrit ''karma'' (action, fate)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"karma (action, deed)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["destiny","fate","karmic"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":42,"contextSentence":"You have to trust in something. Your gut, destiny, life, karma, whatever."},{"word":"dawn","phonetic":"/dɔːn/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"To become evident to the mind; to begin to be perceived or understood","meaningKo":"(깨달음이) 밝아오다, 서서히 알게 되다","etymology":"From Old English ''dagung'' (dawn), related to ''day''","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"dawn (daybreak)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["dawning","dawn on","daybreak"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":57,"contextSentence":"But something slowly began to dawn on me."},{"word":"settle","phonetic":"/ˈsɛtəl/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"To accept something less than ideal or desired; to compromise","meaningKo":"안주하다, 타협하다","etymology":"From Old English ''setlan'' (to place, put)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":null,"root":"settle (sit, place)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["settlement","settled","unsettle"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":74,"contextSentence":"If you haven''t found it yet, keep looking and don''t settle."},{"word":"encounter","phonetic":"/ɪnˈkaʊntər/","partOfSpeech":"verb","definition":"To unexpectedly experience or be faced with something","meaningKo":"마주치다, 접하다","etymology":"From Old French ''encontrer'' (to meet, confront)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"en-","root":"counter (against)","suffix":null},"relatedWords":["encounter","counter","confront"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":82,"contextSentence":"Remembering that I''ll be dead soon is the most important tool I''ve ever encountered."},{"word":"embarrassment","phonetic":"/ɪmˈbærəsmənt/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"A feeling of self-consciousness, shame, or awkwardness","meaningKo":"당혹감, 창피함","etymology":"From French ''embarrasser'' (to block, obstruct)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"em-","root":"barrass (bar, obstruct)","suffix":"-ment"},"relatedWords":["embarrass","embarrassing","embarrassed"],"isEssential":false,"segmentIndex":84,"contextSentence":"All fear of embarrassment or failure, these things just fall away in the face of death."},{"word":"destination","phonetic":"/ˌdɛstɪˈneɪʃən/","partOfSpeech":"noun","definition":"The place to which someone or something is going or being sent","meaningKo":"목적지, 도착지","etymology":"From Latin ''destinare'' (to determine, appoint)","rootBreakdown":{"prefix":"de-","root":"stin (stand, establish)","suffix":"-ation"},"relatedWords":["destiny","destine","predestination"],"isEssential":true,"segmentIndex":88,"contextSentence":"Death is the destination we all share."}]'::jsonb, '[{"pattern":"Conditional Past (If + had + past participle)","explanation":"Used to describe hypothetical situations in the past that did not actually happen. The ''if'' clause uses past perfect, and the main clause uses ''would have + past participle''.","explanationKo":"과거에 실제로 일어나지 않은 가정적 상황을 설명할 때 사용합니다. ''if'' 절은 과거완료형을 사용하고, 주절은 ''would have + 과거분사''를 사용합니다. 제3조건문이라고도 합니다.","examples":["If I had never dropped in on that single course in college, the Mac would have never had multiple typefaces.","If I had never dropped out, I would have never dropped in on that calligraphy class."],"segmentIndex":35},{"pattern":"Gerund as Subject","explanation":"A gerund (-ing form of a verb) used as the subject of a sentence. This structure treats an action as a noun concept.","explanationKo":"동명사(-ing 형태의 동사)를 문장의 주어로 사용하는 구조입니다. 행동을 명사 개념으로 다룹니다.","examples":["Remembering that I''ll be dead soon is the most important tool I''ve ever encountered.","Remembering that you are going to die is the best way I know to avoid the trap.","Believing that the dots will connect down the road will give you the confidence."],"segmentIndex":82},{"pattern":"Parallel Structure (not A but B / A, not B)","explanation":"Using the same grammatical form for elements that are joined by conjunctions or compared. This creates rhythm and clarity in speech.","explanationKo":"접속사로 연결되거나 비교되는 요소에 같은 문법 형태를 사용하는 것입니다. 연설에 리듬감과 명확성을 부여합니다.","examples":["The heaviness of being successful was replaced by the lightness of being a beginner again.","You can''t connect the dots looking forward. You can only connect them looking backwards."],"segmentIndex":60},{"pattern":"Imperative for Motivational Commands","explanation":"The base form of the verb used without a subject to give direct commands, advice, or motivational instructions. Common in speeches to directly address the audience.","explanationKo":"주어 없이 동사 원형을 사용하여 직접적인 명령, 조언, 또는 동기부여 지시를 하는 구조입니다. 청중에게 직접 말할 때 연설에서 흔히 사용됩니다.","examples":["Stay hungry. Stay foolish.","Don''t settle.","Don''t lose faith.","Keep looking."],"segmentIndex":96},{"pattern":"Relative Clause with ''who/that/which''","explanation":"A clause that provides additional information about a noun, using relative pronouns like who, that, or which. Essential for adding detail and complexity to sentences.","explanationKo":"who, that, which 같은 관계대명사를 사용하여 명사에 대한 추가 정보를 제공하는 절입니다. 문장에 세부 사항과 복잡성을 더하는 데 필수적입니다.","examples":["We hired someone who I thought was very talented to run the company with me.","An amazing woman who would become my wife.","Don''t be trapped by dogma, which is living with the results of other people''s thinking."],"segmentIndex":49},{"pattern":"Phrasal Verbs (drop out, drop in, fall away, dawn on)","explanation":"Multi-word verbs consisting of a verb plus a preposition or adverb that creates a meaning different from the original verb. Very common in spoken English.","explanationKo":"동사에 전치사나 부사가 결합되어 원래 동사와 다른 의미를 만드는 복합 동사입니다. 구어 영어에서 매우 일반적으로 사용됩니다.","examples":["I dropped out of Reed College after the first six months.","I could stop taking the required classes and begin dropping in on the ones that looked far more interesting.","Something slowly began to dawn on me.","These things just fall away in the face of death."],"segmentIndex":2},{"pattern":"Rhetorical Question","explanation":"A question asked not to get an answer, but to make a point or create emphasis. Used frequently in speeches to engage the audience.","explanationKo":"대답을 얻기 위해서가 아니라 논점을 강조하거나 만들기 위해 던지는 질문입니다. 청중의 참여를 유도하기 위해 연설에서 자주 사용됩니다.","examples":["So why did I drop out?","How can you get fired from a company you started?","Do you want him?"],"segmentIndex":3},{"pattern":"Passive Voice for Emphasis","explanation":"Using passive construction (be + past participle) to shift focus from the doer to the action or receiver. Often used to emphasize the experience rather than the agent.","explanationKo":"수동태 구문(be + 과거분사)을 사용하여 행위자에서 행동이나 대상으로 초점을 전환합니다. 행위자보다 경험을 강조할 때 자주 사용됩니다.","examples":["The heaviness of being successful was replaced by the lightness of being a beginner again.","All of my working class parents'' savings were being spent on my college tuition.","I''d been rejected, but I was still in love."],"segmentIndex":61},{"pattern":"Superlative for Emphasis","explanation":"Using superlative adjectives (most + adjective or adjective + -est) to express the highest degree, creating powerful emphasis in motivational speech.","explanationKo":"최상급 형용사(most + 형용사 또는 형용사 + -est)를 사용하여 최고의 정도를 표현하며, 동기부여 연설에서 강력한 강조를 만듭니다.","examples":["It was one of the best decisions I ever made.","Remembering that I''ll be dead soon is the most important tool I''ve ever encountered.","Death is very likely the single best invention of life."],"segmentIndex":19},{"pattern":"Correlative Conjunctions (as...as, not only...but)","explanation":"Pairs of conjunctions that work together to join equal grammatical elements. They create balanced, emphatic statements.","explanationKo":"같은 문법 요소를 연결하기 위해 함께 사용되는 접속사 쌍입니다. 균형 잡히고 강조적인 문장을 만듭니다.","examples":["And that is as true for work as it is for your lovers.","A college that was almost as expensive as Stanford."],"segmentIndex":71},{"pattern":"Infinitive of Purpose (to + verb)","explanation":"Using ''to + base verb'' to express the purpose or reason for an action. A fundamental structure for explaining motivations.","explanationKo":"행동의 목적이나 이유를 표현하기 위해 ''to + 동사 원형''을 사용합니다. 동기를 설명하기 위한 기본적인 구조입니다.","examples":["I decided to take a calligraphy class to learn how to do this.","I returned Coke bottles for the five-cent deposits to buy food with.","I would walk the seven miles across town every Sunday night to get one good meal a week."],"segmentIndex":28},{"pattern":"Present Perfect for Life Experience","explanation":"Using ''have/has + past participle'' to describe experiences or actions that happened at an unspecified time in the past and are still relevant now.","explanationKo":"과거의 불특정한 시점에 일어났지만 현재까지 관련이 있는 경험이나 행동을 설명할 때 ''have/has + 과거분사''를 사용합니다.","examples":["If you haven''t found it yet, keep looking.","No one has ever escaped it.","I''ve looked in the mirror every morning and asked myself."],"segmentIndex":74}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"linking","originalText":"dropped out of","phonetic":"/drɑːptˈaʊdəv/","koreanPhonetic":"드랍타우러브","explanation":"The final ''t'' in ''dropped'' links to the vowel ''ou'' in ''out'', and ''out'' links to ''of'' with the ''t'' connecting to the vowel.","explanationKo":"''dropped''의 마지막 ''t''가 ''out''의 모음 ''ou''와 연결되고, ''out''은 ''t''가 ''of''의 모음에 연결됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''드랍-타우-러브''처럼 세 단어를 끊지 않고 자연스럽게 이어서 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":2},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"want to","phonetic":"/ˈwɑːnə/","koreanPhonetic":"워나","explanation":"''Want to'' is commonly reduced to ''wanna'' in casual and natural speech. The ''t'' sounds are dropped entirely.","explanationKo":"''want to''는 일상적이고 자연스러운 말에서 보통 ''wanna''로 축약됩니다. ''t'' 소리가 완전히 탈락합니다.","practiceGuide":"''워나''로 빠르게 발음하세요. ''I wanna tell you'' 처럼 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":0},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"going to","phonetic":"/ˈɡʌnə/","koreanPhonetic":"거나","explanation":"''Going to'' is frequently reduced to ''gonna'' in natural speech, especially when expressing future intentions.","explanationKo":"''going to''는 자연스러운 말에서 자주 ''gonna''로 축약됩니다. 특히 미래 의도를 표현할 때 그렇습니다.","practiceGuide":"''거나''로 빠르게 발음하세요. ''Life''s gonna hit you'' 처럼 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":69},{"type":"linking","originalText":"connect the dots","phonetic":"/kəˈnɛktðəˈdɑːts/","koreanPhonetic":"커넥더닷츠","explanation":"The final ''t'' in ''connect'' links smoothly to ''the'', which is reduced. The phrase flows as one unit.","explanationKo":"''connect''의 마지막 ''t''가 축약된 ''the''로 부드럽게 연결됩니다. 전체 구문이 하나의 단위처럼 흐릅니다.","practiceGuide":"''커넥-더-닷츠''를 하나의 덩어리로 빠르게 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":1},{"type":"elision","originalText":"last minute","phonetic":"/ˈlæsˈmɪnɪt/","koreanPhonetic":"래스미닛","explanation":"The ''t'' at the end of ''last'' is often dropped (elided) before the ''m'' in ''minute'', as both are consonant sounds.","explanationKo":"''last''의 끝에 있는 ''t''가 ''minute''의 ''m'' 앞에서 종종 탈락합니다. 둘 다 자음이기 때문입니다.","practiceGuide":"''래스미닛''처럼 ''t''를 생략하고 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":6},{"type":"assimilation","originalText":"would you","phonetic":"/ˈwʊdʒuː/","koreanPhonetic":"우쥬","explanation":"The ''d'' in ''would'' and the ''y'' in ''you'' combine through assimilation to produce a /dʒ/ sound, like ''j''.","explanationKo":"''would''의 ''d''와 ''you''의 ''y''가 동화 현상으로 합쳐져서 ''j''와 같은 /dʒ/ 소리를 냅니다.","practiceGuide":"''우쥬''처럼 ''d''와 ''y''를 합쳐서 ''j'' 소리로 발음하세요. ''Would you want him?''을 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":80},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"you''ve got to","phonetic":"/juːvˈɡɑːɾə/","koreanPhonetic":"유브가러","explanation":"''Got to'' is reduced to ''gotta'' in natural speech. The ''ve'' is also often barely audible.","explanationKo":"''got to''는 자연스러운 말에서 ''gotta''로 축약됩니다. ''ve''도 거의 들리지 않는 경우가 많습니다.","practiceGuide":"''유브-가러''로 빠르게 발음하세요. ''You''ve gotta find what you love.''를 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":71},{"type":"linking","originalText":"turned out to be","phonetic":"/ˈtɜːrndˈaʊɾəbi/","koreanPhonetic":"턴다우러비","explanation":"The ''d'' in ''turned'' links to the vowel in ''out'', and ''out'' links through a flapped ''t'' to ''to be''. The entire phrase flows continuously.","explanationKo":"''turned''의 ''d''가 ''out''의 모음에 연결되고, ''out''은 플랩 ''t''를 통해 ''to be''로 연결됩니다. 전체 구문이 연속적으로 흐릅니다.","practiceGuide":"''턴-다우-러-비''처럼 끊지 않고 이어서 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":25},{"type":"elision","originalText":"don''t know","phonetic":"/doʊnoʊ/","koreanPhonetic":"도노","explanation":"The ''t'' in ''don''t'' is frequently elided before the ''n'' in ''know'', and the phrase can sound like ''dunno''.","explanationKo":"''don''t''의 ''t''가 ''know''의 ''n'' 앞에서 자주 탈락하여, ''dunno''처럼 들릴 수 있습니다.","practiceGuide":"''도노'' 또는 ''더노''처럼 발음하세요. ''I don''t know what to do''를 빠르게 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":54},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"a lot of","phonetic":"/əˈlɑːɾəv/","koreanPhonetic":"얼라러브","explanation":"The ''t'' in ''lot'' becomes a flap /ɾ/ between vowels, and ''of'' reduces to /əv/. The phrase flows as one unit.","explanationKo":"''lot''의 ''t''가 모음 사이에서 플랩 /ɾ/로 변하고, ''of''는 /əv/로 축약됩니다. 전체가 하나의 단위로 흐릅니다.","practiceGuide":"''얼-라-러브''처럼 빠르게 한 덩어리로 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":72},{"type":"linking","originalText":"figure it out","phonetic":"/ˈfɪɡjərɪɾaʊt/","koreanPhonetic":"피겨리라웃","explanation":"The ''r'' in ''figure'' links to the vowel in ''it'', and the ''t'' in ''it'' becomes a flap before the vowel in ''out''.","explanationKo":"''figure''의 ''r''이 ''it''의 모음에 연결되고, ''it''의 ''t''는 ''out''의 모음 앞에서 플랩으로 변합니다.","practiceGuide":"''피겨-리-라웃''처럼 세 단어를 끊지 않고 이어서 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":16},{"type":"assimilation","originalText":"in the","phonetic":"/ɪnðə/","koreanPhonetic":"인더","explanation":"The ''n'' in ''in'' assimilates with ''the'', with the tongue staying in position for the dental ''th'' sound. The two words blend together.","explanationKo":"''in''의 ''n''이 ''the''와 동화되어 혀가 치음 ''th'' 소리를 위한 위치에 머무릅니다. 두 단어가 함께 섞입니다.","practiceGuide":"''인더''처럼 자연스럽게 연결하세요. ''in the mirror'', ''in the face of death'' 등에서 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":79},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"I would","phonetic":"/aɪd/","koreanPhonetic":"아이드","explanation":"''I would'' contracts to ''I''d'' in natural speech. The ''woul-'' portion is completely dropped.","explanationKo":"''I would''는 자연스러운 말에서 ''I''d''로 축약됩니다. ''woul-'' 부분이 완전히 탈락합니다.","practiceGuide":"''아이드''로 빠르게 발음하세요. ''I''d just turned 30'' 처럼 연습하세요.","segmentIndex":48},{"type":"linking","originalText":"make all the difference","phonetic":"/meɪkˈɔːlðəˈdɪfrəns/","koreanPhonetic":"메이콜더디프런스","explanation":"The ''k'' in ''make'' links directly to the vowel in ''all'', and ''all'' connects smoothly to the reduced ''the''.","explanationKo":"''make''의 ''k''가 ''all''의 모음에 직접 연결되고, ''all''은 축약된 ''the''에 부드럽게 연결됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''메이-콜-더-디프런스''로 하나의 흐름처럼 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":44},{"type":"elision","originalText":"best decisions","phonetic":"/ˈbɛsˈdɪsɪʒənz/","koreanPhonetic":"베스디시전즈","explanation":"The ''t'' in ''best'' is often elided before the ''d'' in ''decisions'', as the tongue moves directly from ''s'' to ''d''.","explanationKo":"''best''의 ''t''가 ''decisions''의 ''d'' 앞에서 종종 탈락합니다. 혀가 ''s''에서 바로 ''d''로 이동하기 때문입니다.","practiceGuide":"''베스-디시전즈''처럼 ''t''를 생략하고 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":19},{"type":"reduction","originalText":"kind of","phonetic":"/ˈkaɪndə/","koreanPhonetic":"카인다","explanation":"''Kind of'' is often reduced to ''kinda'' in casual speech. The ''of'' reduces to just a schwa sound.","explanationKo":"''kind of''는 일상 대화에서 ''kinda''로 축약되는 경우가 많습니다. ''of''가 슈와 소리로만 축약됩니다.","practiceGuide":"''카인다''로 빠르게 발음하세요.","segmentIndex":0}]'::jsonb, '{"sections":[{"section":"Introduction","startSegment":0,"endSegment":1,"summary":"Steve Jobs opens by stating he will share three stories from his life, setting a simple and direct tone for the speech.","summaryKo":"스티브 잡스가 자신의 인생에서 세 가지 이야기를 나누겠다고 말하며, 연설의 간결하고 직접적인 톤을 설정합니다.","keyPoints":["세 가지 이야기 구조 제시","겸손하고 친근한 도입"]},{"section":"Story 1: Connecting the Dots - Birth & Adoption","startSegment":1,"endSegment":12,"summary":"Jobs shares the story of his adoption, explaining how his biological mother wanted him raised by college graduates, and the circumstances that led to his adoption by his parents.","summaryKo":"잡스가 입양 이야기를 나누며, 생모가 대학 졸업자에 의해 양육되기를 원했던 것과 부모님에게 입양되기까지의 상황을 설명합니다.","keyPoints":["생모의 입양 결정","입양 부모의 대학 진학 약속","운명적인 시작"]},{"section":"Story 1: Connecting the Dots - Dropping Out","startSegment":13,"endSegment":25,"summary":"Jobs describes his decision to drop out of Reed College due to the financial burden and lack of direction, and how dropping in on classes he enjoyed (like calligraphy) proved valuable later.","summaryKo":"잡스가 재정적 부담과 방향 부재로 리드 대학을 중퇴한 결정과, 서예 같은 좋아하는 수업에 청강한 것이 나중에 가치 있는 것으로 입증된 과정을 설명합니다.","keyPoints":["등록금 부담으로 인한 중퇴 결정","청강생으로서의 경험","호기심과 직감을 따르는 삶"]},{"section":"Story 1: Connecting the Dots - Calligraphy & Mac","startSegment":26,"endSegment":38,"summary":"Jobs connects his calligraphy education at Reed to the typography of the Macintosh, showing how seemingly unrelated experiences became foundational to Apple''s innovation.","summaryKo":"잡스가 리드에서의 서예 교육을 매킨토시의 타이포그래피와 연결하며, 관련 없어 보이는 경험이 애플의 혁신의 기반이 된 과정을 보여줍니다.","keyPoints":["서예 수업의 영향","매킨토시의 아름다운 타이포그래피","예상치 못한 연결"]},{"section":"Story 1: Connecting the Dots - Lesson","startSegment":39,"endSegment":44,"summary":"Jobs delivers the key lesson: you cannot connect the dots looking forward, only backward. You must trust that things will work out, follow your heart, and believe the dots will connect.","summaryKo":"잡스가 핵심 교훈을 전달합니다: 앞을 보며 점을 연결할 수 없고, 뒤돌아볼 때만 가능합니다. 모든 것이 잘 될 것을 믿고, 마음을 따르고, 점들이 연결될 것을 믿어야 합니다.","keyPoints":["점 연결은 뒤돌아볼 때만 가능","직감과 마음을 신뢰하라","잘 닦인 길을 벗어나는 용기"]},{"section":"Story 2: Love and Loss - Apple''s Rise","startSegment":45,"endSegment":52,"summary":"Jobs recounts building Apple from a garage to a $2 billion company, then being fired at age 30 after a power struggle with the board of directors.","summaryKo":"잡스가 차고에서 시작해 20억 달러 회사로 애플을 키운 후, 이사회와의 권력 다툼 끝에 30세에 해고된 이야기를 전합니다.","keyPoints":["차고에서 시작한 애플의 성장","경영진 갈등","30세에 해고"]},{"section":"Story 2: Love and Loss - Devastation & Recovery","startSegment":53,"endSegment":68,"summary":"Jobs describes the devastation of being fired, how he considered leaving Silicon Valley, but eventually started NeXT and Pixar, and returned to Apple through a remarkable turn of events.","summaryKo":"잡스가 해고의 충격, 실리콘 밸리를 떠나려 했던 것, 결국 넥스트와 픽사를 시작한 것, 그리고 놀라운 반전으로 애플에 복귀한 과정을 설명합니다.","keyPoints":["해고의 충격과 좌절","넥스트와 픽사 설립","애플 복귀와 르네상스"]},{"section":"Story 2: Love and Loss - Lesson","startSegment":69,"endSegment":76,"summary":"Jobs shares the lesson: don''t lose faith, find what you love, and don''t settle. Great work comes from loving what you do, and this applies to careers and relationships alike.","summaryKo":"잡스가 교훈을 나눕니다: 신념을 잃지 말고, 사랑하는 것을 찾고, 안주하지 마세요. 위대한 일은 하는 일을 사랑하는 데서 나오며, 이는 직업과 관계 모두에 적용됩니다.","keyPoints":["사랑하는 일을 찾으라","안주하지 말라","위대한 일은 사랑에서 나온다"]},{"section":"Story 3: Death - Living with Awareness","startSegment":77,"endSegment":86,"summary":"Jobs shares how confronting mortality shaped his daily decisions. He describes his habit of asking whether he would still want to do today''s activities if it were his last day.","summaryKo":"잡스가 죽음에 대한 인식이 일상의 결정을 어떻게 형성했는지 나눕니다. 오늘이 마지막 날이라면 오늘의 활동을 여전히 하고 싶은지 묻는 습관을 설명합니다.","keyPoints":["매일 거울 앞에서의 질문","죽음 앞에서 사라지는 두려움","이미 잃을 것이 없다는 깨달음"]},{"section":"Story 3: Death - Death as Life''s Invention","startSegment":87,"endSegment":91,"summary":"Jobs reflects on death as life''s greatest invention and change agent, clearing out the old to make way for the new.","summaryKo":"잡스가 죽음을 생명의 가장 위대한 발명이자 변화의 동력으로 성찰하며, 낡은 것을 치우고 새것을 위한 자리를 만드는 것으로 설명합니다.","keyPoints":["죽음은 생명의 변화 동력","낡은 것을 치우고 새것을 위한 자리","삶의 순환"]},{"section":"Conclusion - Follow Your Heart","startSegment":92,"endSegment":96,"summary":"Jobs concludes with his most powerful advice: don''t waste time living someone else''s life, don''t be trapped by dogma, follow your heart and intuition, and stay hungry, stay foolish.","summaryKo":"잡스가 가장 강력한 조언으로 마무리합니다: 다른 사람의 인생을 사는 데 시간을 낭비하지 말고, 독단에 갇히지 말고, 마음과 직감을 따르고, 항상 갈망하고 우직하게 나아가세요.","keyPoints":["시간 낭비하지 말라","독단에 갇히지 말라","마음과 직감을 따르라","Stay hungry. Stay foolish."]}],"signalExpressions":[{"expression":"Today I want to tell you three stories from my life.","type":"hook","segmentIndex":0,"role":"연설의 구조를 미리 알려주는 도입부. 청중에게 세 가지 이야기를 예고하여 기대감을 형성합니다."},{"expression":"The first story is about connecting the dots.","type":"transition","segmentIndex":1,"role":"첫 번째 이야기로의 전환. 주제를 명확히 제시하여 청중이 따라갈 수 있도록 합니다."},{"expression":"Let me give you one example.","type":"transition","segmentIndex":25,"role":"추상적인 주장에서 구체적인 사례로 전환. 청중의 이해를 돕기 위한 신호입니다."},{"expression":"Again, you can''t connect the dots looking forward.","type":"transition","segmentIndex":40,"role":"핵심 메시지를 반복하여 강조하는 전환 표현. 이야기에서 교훈으로 넘어가는 신호입니다."},{"expression":"My second story is about love and loss.","type":"transition","segmentIndex":45,"role":"두 번째 이야기로의 전환. 새로운 주제를 명확히 제시합니다."},{"expression":"In a remarkable turn of events","type":"transition","segmentIndex":66,"role":"이야기의 극적인 반전을 알리는 전환 표현. 청중의 관심을 다시 집중시킵니다."},{"expression":"If you haven''t found it yet, keep looking and don''t settle.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":74,"role":"두 번째 이야기의 핵심 교훈을 전달하는 결론 표현. 청중에게 직접적인 조언을 합니다."},{"expression":"My third story is about death.","type":"transition","segmentIndex":77,"role":"세 번째이자 마지막 이야기로의 전환. 가장 무거운 주제를 담담하게 소개합니다."},{"expression":"Your time is limited, so don''t waste it living someone else''s life.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":92,"role":"연설의 최종 메시지를 전달하는 결론부. 모든 이야기를 하나의 교훈으로 종합합니다."},{"expression":"Stay hungry. Stay foolish.","type":"conclusion","segmentIndex":96,"role":"연설의 마지막 문장이자 가장 유명한 인용구. 간결하면서도 강렬한 마무리로 청중에게 깊은 인상을 남깁니다."}]}'::jsonb
)
